  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Mobile Viewer App**\n\nI\'m currently focused on creating a mobile app that allows users to view DWG drawings directly on their smartphones. I\'ve received some code, `/public/assets/aistudio/index_c6b94c45.html`, that I\'ll be using as the basis. My immediate goal is to adapt this code for a personal distribution app. I\'m exploring the nuances of the code.\n\n\n**Analyzing CAD Viewer Features**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously examining the features of the mobile CAD viewer code. It\'s truly comprehensive, handling DWG and DXF parsing entirely client-side. The integration with LibreDWG WebAssembly is impressive, along with the fallback options and the handling of complex geometric transformations. I\'m paying close attention to the Korean text decoding capabilities and the OSNAP features as I consider adapting this code.\n\n\n**Refining Feature Implementation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific enhancements for the mobile viewer. The key is to improve measurement accuracy on smartphones, especially with a precision touch loupe to avoid finger occlusion. I\'m prioritizing 2-point scale calibration and also a powerful layer manager, with a text search modal. I\'m also considering a minimap and theme options, and developing seamless installation for personal distribution and embedding with active CAD drawing data.\n\n\n**Structuring Mobile CAD App**\n\nI\'m now diving into the React/Vite app structure. I\'m aiming for a production-ready React application within `src/`, integrating the existing features. I\'m focusing on PWA offline support with `vite-plugin-pwa`, `PWAInstallButton`, local file caching via IndexedDB, touch gestures, and high-DPI canvas rendering. My priority is also measurement tools, layer management, and personal app features.\n\n\n"
