  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Canvas Features**\n\nI\'m currently focused on implementing the canvas view capture on drawing file opening and storing it in local storage. I\'m also working to display thumbnails of recently opened drawings and their last accessed times within the file selection modal. These additions should enhance usability.\n\n\n**Refining Storage Mechanisms**\n\nI\'m now refining how I will store the canvas view as a thumbnail and its associated metadata. The focus is on efficiently storing these thumbnails in either `localStorage` or `IndexedDB`. Each recent drawing item will store a unique ID, filename, timestamp, and the thumbnail itself. I\'m investigating how best to generate lightweight thumbnails for quick display in the file selection modal, to improve user experience.\n\n\n**Optimizing Data Storage**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on optimizing data storage for recent drawings. To avoid exceeding `localStorage` limits, I\'ll scale thumbnails down to around 240x160 pixels, ensuring they\'re lightweight. Actual drawing data will be cached using IndexedDB, allowing fast re-opening. A hybrid approach seems best, with thumbnail metadata mirrored in both `localStorage` and IndexedDB.\n\n\n**Defining Data Schema**\n\nI\'m solidifying the data schema for recent drawings. I plan to store `formatVersion`, `entityCount`, `layerCount`, and `lastOpenedAt` in `localStorage` or IndexedDB. The full `DrawingModel` itself will reside in IndexedDB, which should give near-instant loading times from recent drawings. Users will be able to remove items from the recent list or clear all entries.\n\n**Enhancing File Selection**\n\nI\'m focused on the user interface now, planning to incorporate a \"Recent Drawings\" section in the file selection modal, and the empty state welcome screen. Thumbnail cards will display the last access time, entity count, and file format, along with a click-to-open function. I\'m exploring adding a \"Recent Drawings\" button in the header too.\n\n\n"
