    thinking: "**Analyzing Layout Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on the layout structure defined within the JSX code, specifically lines 479 and 506. I\'m noting the use of flexbox for the overall screen dimensions and the relative positioning of the content area with an embedded CADCanvas component. I\'m now diving into the CADCanvas component itself to understand how the internal rendering works.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile View Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the mobile view implementation. I\'ve pinpointed an issue with `h-screen` and `100vh` in mobile browsers, especially during orientation changes. The suggested solution involves utilizing `w-full h-full h-[100dvh] flex flex-col overflow-hidden` for dynamic resizing. I\'m cross-referencing this approach within `App.tsx` and `CADCanvas.tsx` to ensure consistency. The `handleResize` function in `CADCanvas.tsx` is my next target, to ensure the resizing is also properly handled.\n\n\n**Observing Canvas Updates**\n\nI\'m now deeply involved in the intricacies of the `CADCanvas` component\'s rendering logic. Specifically, I\'ve noted that direct manipulation of `canvas.width` and `canvas.height` doesn\'t trigger a React re-render. Consequently, the canvas can blank itself, or fail to apply height changes. This means that a `ResizeObserver` is vital to correctly handle size updates to the canvas, and I\'m figuring out how to implement it correctly, especially in `useEffect`. I\'m going to look more into `prevH` and `prevW`, which I see may be used to handle resize updates!\n\n\n**Implementing Size Observer**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the implementation details for size updates, with a focus on the `ResizeObserver` and its associated event listeners. I\'m taking a close look at the `updateSize` function, which determines size changes and forces a re-render using `setCanvasDimensions`. I\'m especially interested in handling orientation changes correctly. I\'m now testing the code with different window dimensions and orientations to identify and fix any issues.\n\n\n**Refining Portrait Orientation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on handling orientation changes, especially when the aspect ratio flips. I\'m focusing on ensuring the drawing automatically centers and fits the new screen dimensions. My goal is to ensure that a drawing, if present, remains visible and correctly scaled when the screen switches between landscape and portrait views. I\'m focusing on making a good user experience.\n\n\n**Adding Menu Control**\n\nI\'m now implementing the ability to hide the menu bars, as requested. I\'ve introduced `isMenuHidden` in `App.tsx` to manage the state and added corresponding buttons with icons in `Header.tsx` and the floating pill of `CADCanvas.tsx`. These buttons will toggle the visibility of the top `Header`, `UniversalModeBar`, and bottom `BottomDock` components, expanding the canvas container to 100% when hidden. The UI interactions and animation will be considered. I need to make sure the state is correct, and that the UI handles the change correctly.\n\n\n"
