  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Canvas Dimensions**\n\nI\'ve initiated the dimensional setup in `CADCanvas.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m integrating state to control canvas dimensions, initializing them to 400x600. I am also implementing a ref to store a portrait-mode boolean, tentatively titled `prevIsPortraitRef`. This feels like a good first step.\n\n\n**Implementing ResizeObserver**\n\nI\'m now integrating `ResizeObserver` within `CADCanvas.tsx` to dynamically manage canvas dimensions. A `useEffect` hook monitors the container\'s size, updating the canvas\'s width and height accordingly, ensuring it never goes below 100x100. This also updates the `canvasDimensions` state. Furthermore, it incorporates an auto-adjustment for the camera when switching between landscape and portrait orientations.\n\n\n**Refining Auto-Adjustments**\n\nI\'m currently refining the auto-adjustment of the camera within the resize handler. I\'m focusing on calculating new camera positions (newCamX, newCamY) and fitted zoom levels to ensure the rendered elements stay within the new canvas dimensions. Crucially, I\'ve added a dependency to the render useEffect so render always runs with changes.\n\n\n**Adding Menu Control Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating menu visibility controls. I\'ve introduced `isMenuHidden` and `onToggleMenuHidden` to manage the menu\'s state and provide a toggle function. I\'ve added a floating button in the top-left to show the menu when it\'s hidden. Additionally, a toggle button has been integrated into the right-hand pill to provide intuitive menu control.\n\n\n"
