  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **User Request**: Add Google Drive and Dropbox integration to the mobile CAD (DWG/DXF) viewer app. Users must be able to log in with their cloud accounts, directly browse and open their DWG/DXF drawing files from Google Drive and Dropbox, and manage their cloud drawings within the viewer.\n   - **Scope Boundaries**:\n     - Google Drive integration requires Google Workspace OAuth via `set_up_oauth` tool (following the `workspace-integration` skill). Client-side OAuth with Firebase Auth (already supported in AI Studio template) and Google Drive API v3.\n     - Dropbox integration requires OAuth flow (or Dropbox Chooser / PKCE OAuth via client token) with client-side file fetch.\n     - Files fetched from cloud must feed into the existing client-side LibreDWG/DXF parser pipeline (`applyDrawingModel`), saving to local recent list / IndexedDB cache with auto-generated canvas thumbnail.\n   - **Mandatory OAuth Protocol (workspace-integration)**:\n     - `set_up_oauth` MUST be called first with `userConfirmedInUI: false` and the specific scopes (`https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly` or `drive.file`), then STOP the conversation immediately to wait for user acceptance.\n     - Once accepted, call `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: true`, then implement code.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed in earlier turns**:\n     - Full client-side mobile DWG/DXF viewer with LibreDWG WebAssembly and DXF parser (`src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts`, `src/lib/dxfParser.ts`, `src/lib/modelExpander.ts`).\n     - PWA integration configured with `vite-plugin-pwa` and manifest icons (`public/icon.svg`, `pwa-192x192.png`, `pwa-512x512.png`).\n     - Canvas view thumbnail capture and IndexedDB/localStorage caching (`src/lib/drawingStorage.ts`).\n     - Fullscreen immersive mode / menu hide toggle (`isMenuHidden`) and dynamic viewport height auto-resizing (`100dvh`, `ResizeObserver`).\n     - File selection and recent drawings modal (`src/components/FileSelectModal.tsx`).\n   - **Just Inspected**:\n     - Read `/skills/system_skills/workspace_integration/SKILL.md` to review the required Google Drive OAuth workflow.\n   - **In Progress**:\n     - Need to initiate `set_up_oauth` tool call with `userConfirmedInUI: false` for Google Drive (`https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly`).\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - Google Drive integration requires OAuth scope: `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly` (or `drive.file` if saving/exporting back to drive).\n   - Calling `set_up_oauth` will automatically provision Firebase Auth for sign-in and produce `firebase-applet-config.json`.\n   - Workspace skill rule: \"The agent MUST NOT call any other tool or write code until it has called `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: false`, stopped, waited for confirmation, and called it again with `userConfirmedInUI: true`.\"\n   - Dropbox integration: Can use client-side PKCE OAuth or Dropbox API token / Chooser. Can be configured alongside or in a Cloud Storage panel.\n   - File fetching: Google Drive API `GET https://www.googleapis.com/drive/v3/files/{fileId}?alt=media` with `Authorization: Bearer <token>` returns arrayBuffer, which can directly be passed to `parseBinaryDwgFile` or `parseDxfText`.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - Past Turn: TS7006 implicit any on `(e: any): e is CadEntity` in `libreDwgLoader.ts` -> Fixed.\n   - Past Turn: TS1005 missing parenthesis on `forwardRef` in `CADCanvas.tsx` -> Fixed.\n   - Past Turn: Portrait mode half-screen black rendering due to missing flex context and `ResizeObserver` -> Fixed by adding `100dvh`, `ResizeObserver`, and auto-fit on orientation change.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Current turn received the user request for Google Drive & Dropbox integration.\n   - `workspace-integration` skill is actively relevant.\n   - No code edits have been made yet for this new feature.\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. **Turn 1 (Immediate Next Action)**:\n      - Call `set_up_oauth` with:\n        - `scopes_to_add: [\"https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly\"]`\n        - `title: \"Google Drive \353\217\204\353\251\264 \355\214\214\354\235\274 \352\260\200\354\240\270\354\230\244\352\270\260\"`\n        - `userConfirmedInUI: false`\n      - Provide a user-facing explanation in Korean mentioning the full product name (\"Google Drive\"), the capability (browse and open DWG/DXF files with permission), and telling the user to review the card below to connect Google Drive. Stop immediately.\n   2. **Turn 2 (After User Confirms)**:\n      - Call `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: true` and the scopes.\n      - Install `firebase` package if not present (`npm i firebase`).\n      - Create `src/lib/googleDrive.ts` using Firebase Auth Google provider (`new GoogleAuthProvider()` with drive scope) and Drive v3 REST API to list DWG/DXF files (`name contains \'.dwg\' or name contains \'.dxf\'`) and download binary content (`alt=media`).\n      - Create `src/lib/dropbox.ts` for Dropbox authentication/file listing & download.\n      - Update `FileSelectModal.tsx` or create a new `CloudStorageModal.tsx` / tabs in `FileSelectModal.tsx` (\"\353\202\264 \352\270\260\352\270\260\", \"\354\265\234\352\267\274 \353\217\204\353\251\264\", \"Google Drive\", \"Dropbox\") displaying authenticated account info, cloud file explorer, file size, last modified date, and click-to-open directly in the viewer.\n      - Verify with `lint_applet` and `compile_applet`.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Must strictly follow `workspace-integration` 2-turn protocol: call `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: false`, wait for user approval, call with `userConfirmedInUI: true` before writing any Drive code.\n   - Do NOT store OAuth access tokens in `localStorage` or `sessionStorage` (in-memory caching only).\n   - Real integrations with clean UI (no fake mock data, use real OAuth/API calls).\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_end: 212
    render_latest_checkpoint: true
    total_subagent_count: 0
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
