  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Requirements**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on the user\'s specific request. It\'s clear they want a DWG viewer app for smartphones with Google Drive and Dropbox integration. The key is allowing users to log in with their cloud accounts and directly access, open, and manage their DWG files within the app. I am parsing their needs.\n\n\n**Implementing Google Drive**\n\nI\'m making progress on Google Drive integration now. I have the Firebase setup, including the API key and app ID. The OAuth scope for read-only access is in place. I have begun implementing the Firebase initialization and OAuth provider configuration, following the provided steps. I\'m focusing on the login flow and file retrieval next.\n\n\n**Integrating the Drive API**\n\nI\'ve got the Google Drive API calls mapped out. I understand I need to use the `accessToken` obtained during login. I now know I must list files by querying the Drive API with the appropriate query parameters (filtering by extension and mimeType), and download them using the file ID and the authorization header. I\'m considering folder browsing and filename search features as well.\n\n\n**Considering Token Storage**\n\nI\'m now focusing on secure token storage. I\'m taking the requirement to avoid `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` seriously. I\'m investigating in-memory token storage strategies for both Google Drive and Dropbox integrations. I am also investigating handling the Dropbox OAuth 2.0 PKCE flow, which would be ideal. I\'m exploring how to make use of Dropbox Chooser JS API securely. I\'m also planning to support direct links.\n\n\n**Designing the UI**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user interface. I\'m building a \"Cloud Storage Explorer\" within the app. I plan to add a prominent tab or button to the header, possibly with Google Drive and Dropbox logos. The user should be able to easily browse their cloud files and download test drawings. I plan to use direct links. I also want to incorporate convenient Dropbox link importing with URL auto-parsing. The app will list files from Dropbox using API calls and allow file downloading directly. I plan to store connection settings securely.\n\n\n"
