  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring UI Options**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `Header.tsx` and considering a cloud storage icon or button within it. Alternatively, I\'m thinking users could click \"\353\217\204\353\251\264 \354\227\264\352\270\260\" to launch `FileSelectModal.tsx`. The modal now has refined tabs: \"\353\202\264 \352\270\260\352\270\260 & \354\265\234\352\267\274\" (My Device & Recent Drawings) and \"Google\".\n\n\n**Implementing Cloud Integration**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation details for Google Drive and Dropbox integration. For Google Drive, I\'m leaning heavily on Firebase Auth within `src/lib/googleDrive.ts`, planning to store the `accessToken` in memory. I am creating functions for `initFirebaseDrive()` and `signInGoogleDrive()` using the `GoogleAuthProvider`. I\'ll be exploring the specific scopes required for accessing and managing Google Drive files.\n\n\n**Refining Google Drive Access**\n\nI\'ve been working on refining Google Drive access methods. I\'ve implemented `signInGoogleDrive()` with `select_account` prompt and plan to manage the access token. I am currently fleshing out `signOutGoogleDrive()` and have started `getGoogleUser()`. I\'m building `listGoogleDriveFiles()` using the Drive API, filtering for CAD file types and handling pagination.\n\n\n**Developing Dropbox Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on Dropbox integration, specifically how to handle direct shared links. I\'ve realized that modifying the `dl=0` parameter to `dl=1` or `raw=1` in Dropbox shared links allows direct downloading of DWG/DXF files as an ArrayBuffer using `fetch()`. This avoids authentication, enabling immediate file opening in the canvas. I\'m keen on building this feature.\n\n\n**Integrating Dropbox Access**\n\nI\'m now integrating Dropbox API v2. I\'m focusing on user account connection via Access Token or App Token, possibly OAuth PKCE. I have outlined the process of listing files in a folder using the `files/list_folder` endpoint, filtering for DWG and DXF files. I\'m also preparing to download these files using the `files/download` endpoint, which should return an ArrayBuffer. I\'m also exploring the Dropbox Chooser SDK and considering it as a fallback. I plan to offer both shared link import, a personal access token connection and, optionally, folder access.\n\n\n"
