  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Network Failures**\n\nI\'m currently delving into the root causes of the `auth/network-request-failed` error that surfaces during Firebase Auth\'s `signInWithPopup` process. My investigation has led me to scrutinize the error stack, and specifically the connection between Firebase authentication and Google Drive sign-in issues. I\'m focusing on why a network failure might manifest within the Firebase framework, even when signing in with Google.\n\n\n**Investigating Firebase Popup**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on Firebase Auth\'s `signInWithPopup` process and its potential network failure origins. The stack trace points me towards examining the `authDomain` and its interaction with `gen-lang-client-0401838453.firebaseapp.com/__/auth/handler`. I am now checking to see if Firebase Identity Platform (Auth) is enabled, or if CORS/authorized domains are configured. My next question: Can we support Google Identity Services token client?\n\n\n**Examining App Configuration**\n\nI\'ve just reviewed the `firebase-applet-config.json` file. Key observations include the `oAuthClientId` and the `authDomain`, which I\'m now cross-referencing with environment constraints. It\'s becoming clearer that Firebase Auth\'s `signInWithPopup` uses `window.open` for cross-origin communication with `authDomain`, which is essential and should be verified. The environment constraints highlight a potential conflict with popup usage, since I have `port 3000 & iFrame: Dev server must run on port 3000. Avoid window.alert/window.open.`, and this function calls Firebase Identity Toolkit.\n\n\n"
