    thinking: "**Examining Authorization Details**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that `access-control-allow-origin: https://ais-dev-p55zubkq37ae52rlsf5zht-920363950371.asia-east1.run.app` is permitted. My focus has shifted to the POST body now. I need to determine what occurred after the popup closed, and I\'m currently looking into `PopupOperation.onAuthEvent`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Network Blockage**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implications of potential network blockages. Specifically, I\'m examining how ad blockers, like AdGuard and uBlock Origin, and even Brave Shields, might be interfering with `identitytoolkit.googleapis.com`. It appears these blockers often classify it as a tracking domain, which could trigger `auth/network-request-failed` errors. I\'m also considering the impact of disabled third-party cookies on the process.\n\n\n**Clarifying Token Acquisition Methods**\n\nI\'m now clarifying how Google Identity Services (GIS) directly provides the OAuth `access_token`, bypassing ad blockers and third-party cookie restrictions, as it\'s Google\'s first-party client. This means that we can directly obtain the `access_token` that\'s needed for the Google Drive API, skipping Firebase Auth entirely. The need for Firebase Auth is thus reduced to an intermediary step to obtain the `access_token`.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Token Acquisition**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the best method for getting that critical `access_token` - the Google-recommended `initTokenClient` from GIS is the modern standard! I\'m planning a multi-layered authentication strategy. First, I\'ll attempt the GIS Token Client using the specified `oAuthClientId` and scope, calling `tokenClient.requestAccessToken({ prompt: \'\' })`. I\'m going to get the user info immediately to confirm login before executing other logic. If that fails, as a fallback, I will use Firebase Auth `signInWithPopup`.\n\n\n"
