  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining User Structure**\n\nI\'m currently working on defining a more structured `GoogleAuthUser` interface in `src/lib/googleDrive.ts`. Right now, I\'m working with the `User | null` type from `firebase/auth`. I believe a clearer interface is needed, and I\'m planning to use `displayName`, `email`, and `photoURL` as the key properties.\n\n\n**Examining Login Flow**\n\nI\'m now diving into the login flow, specifically the \"Google Drive \353\241\234\352\267\270\354\235\270\" process. I\'m focusing on how Google Identity Services is utilized, or loaded if it isn\'t readily available. I\'m also examining how the OAuth2 token client is initialized, and how we fetch the user profile data using the access token after successful authentication.\n\n\n**Analyzing Authentication Failures**\n\nI\'ve just refined the error handling for authentication, focusing on cases where Google Identity Services (GIS) fails or is blocked. I\'ve noted that `auth/network-request-failed` won\'t happen. If GIS fails, I\'ll attempt Firebase Auth\'s popup. A network failure here triggers a user-friendly Korean message. We offer direct Google Drive link opening, access token input, and a Dropbox link as backup options.\n\n\n**Exploring Shared Link Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `downloadFromGoogleDriveSharedLink` function. I\'m focusing on parsing Google Drive shared links and file IDs. I\'ve written a function to extract the file ID from various link formats, including those with `view` parameters or direct file IDs. This will allow for direct downloading.\n\n\n"
