    thinking: "**Analyzing Code Dependencies**\n\nOkay, I\'m deep diving into `libreDwgLoader.ts`, `dxfParser.ts`, and `modelExpander.ts`. The focus is on the long line issue the user mentioned. I\'m trying to figure out why these lines are showing up in the imported drawings. I\'m looking at how these three files interact during the import process.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Entity Mishandling**\n\nI\'ve homed in on a potential culprit: the `DIMENSION` entity handling within `libreDwgLoader.ts`. The code suggests a broad approach to dimension types. I\'m scrutinizing how these are interpreted and rendered. My hunch is that this general handling might be misinterpreting or mis-rendering certain dimension types as long lines. I\'ll test specific cases related to the screenshots.\n\n\n**Revisiting Coordinate Systems**\n\nI\'ve circled back to the coordinate systems, specifically how `DIMENSION` entities are handled. I\'m focusing on the discrepancy between DXF/DWG specifications \342\200\223 the anonymous block entities are already in WCS \342\200\223 and how we\'re interpreting and positioning them in `libreDwgLoader.ts`. The `ent.position = wIns;` line looks problematic as the original DXF position has been set to 0,0. It seems the positioning logic might be incorrectly re-transforming these already world-coordinate entities, which can result in incorrectly placed entities with large coordinates.\n\n\n**Fixing Position Logic**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a crucial issue in handling dimension entities. The insertion point is being incorrectly used. Specifically, the line `ent.position = wIns` is causing a translation error. This is because the `insertionPoint` in this context refers to the dimension text position, not the block insertion point, which should be (0, 0). Consequently, lines and arrows within dimension blocks are being doubly transformed, creating those excessively long lines. This affects dimension lines, projection lines, and extension lines, shifting them across the drawing.\n\n\n**Addressing Invisible Entities**\n\nI\'ve discovered the rendering issue stems from not considering invisible entities. The code needs an update to explicitly check for `raw.invisible`, `raw.invis`, `raw.is_invisible`, or `raw.visibility === 1` before rendering. The DXF parser also needs to check group code 60. I must now focus on applying these checks to ensure hidden entities are not inadvertently displayed.\n\n\n\n**Investigating Streak Artifacts**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a segment in `modelExpander.ts`, specifically the `isArtifactStreakSegment` function. I\'ve analyzed its logic in relation to the reported artifact. It seems that the current implementation doesn\'t effectively filter very long, non-diagonal segments, especially those crossing sub-views in mechanical drawings. This oversight could be the source of the streak. My focus now is on refining the filtering criteria within this function to correctly identify and remove these problematic segments.\n\n**Refining Streak Filtering**\n\nI\'m now implementing a new check to address streak artifacts, focusing on closed polylines. I\'m focusing on the length of a closing segment relative to the average segment length within the polyline. The goal is to identify and correct false polyline closures where the closing segment drastically exceeds the average segment length, which indicates a jump across the drawing. My analysis includes length comparison to the drawing\'s span.\n\n\n**Examining Data Sources**\n\nI\'m now assessing how entities are gathered from both `db.entities` and `BLOCK_RECORD` in `libreDwgLoader.ts`, specifically around lines 595-655. It seems there\'s a priority order being considered and I\'m looking at how the `*MODEL_SPACE` blocks and their entity content are handled. I need to understand whether we are correctly prioritizing the data from `db.entities` over the `BLOCK_RECORD` entries when populating the model. The code handling the fallback `modelSpaceFallback` needs careful scrutiny to ensure that model space entities are not duplicated or incorrectly prioritized, which could affect how lines are ultimately rendered.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Entity Sorting**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a critical section within `libreDwgLoader.ts`, specifically lines 595-655, where entity processing occurs. I see a potential issue where entities are being duplicated from ModelSpace and PaperSpace. The core problem is accurately differentiating between ModelSpace and PaperSpace entities. My focus is on ensuring `db.entities` data is correctly filtered for ModelSpace, and that PaperSpace entities, indicated by properties such as `r.in_paperspace` or `r.paperspace`, are correctly excluded to prevent rendering issues.\n\n\n**Implementing PaperSpace Filtering**\n\nI\'m now implementing a PaperSpace filter within `libreDwgLoader.ts` to prevent overlapping artifacts. I\'ve added a check to exclude entities marked as `raw.in_paperspace === 1`, `raw.paperspace === 1`, or `raw.in_paperspace === true`. This should resolve the overlap of ModelSpace entities with PaperSpace frames and projection lines. My analysis ensures that the ModelSpace drawing will render correctly by excluding PaperSpace entities when viewing model space.\n\n**Enhancing Theme System**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to theme system enhancement, based on a new request. I\'ve examined `src/types/cad.ts`, and `src/App.tsx`, and `UniversalModeBar.tsx`. I\'m now exploring how to integrate system dark mode detection, in order to dynamically adjust the UI theme. The plan is to enhance the theme system such that the UI theme automatically changes according to the system\'s dark mode setting.\n\n\n**Integrating System Theme Detection**\n\nI\'m now implementing automatic dark mode support, focusing on system theme detection within the app. I\'m leveraging `window.matchMedia(\'(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\')` to detect the system\'s preferred color scheme upon app load. I am also using `useEffect` with `window.matchMedia` to listen for system theme changes and update the UI accordingly. I\'ll need to account for user-overridden preferences in local storage. The system auto setting will be the default if there are no other overrides. I need to make the change dynamically.\n\n\n"
