  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing CAD Elements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the `isArtifactStreakSegment` function and false polyline closure within `modelExpander.ts`. I\'m trying to determine the conditions that trigger long horizontal/vertical lines in CAD drawings, particularly lines exceeding a certain length threshold. The goal is to understand the root cause.\n\n\n**Refining Artifact Detection**\n\nI\'ve been refining the criteria for identifying artifact streaks. I\'ve considered that lines exceeding 40% of the drawing span are only legitimate in specific contexts: the outer title block border or grid/axis lines on dedicated layers. I\'m focusing on scenarios where a horizontal or vertical line (defined by a small `dy` or `dx` relative to its length) is *not* near the border and exceeds a certain length threshold\342\200\224this is likely an artifact. The Polyline Closure is being inspected.\n\n\n**Evaluating Polyline Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the internal logic of polyline handling, specifically how we determine false closures and internal jump segments. I\'m excited by how we identify and correct falsely closed polylines, using the median segment length and a distance check relative to the drawing span. This helps us catch connections of things that should be separate (e.g., that vertical streak). I\'m also examining the criteria for detecting internal jump segments within a polyline.\n\n\n**Investigating Subpath Jumps**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on a critical condition: `segLen > Math.max(medianStep * 15, 200)` AND `segLen > Math.min(spanW, spanH) * 0.18`. This has led me to identify a disconnected subpath jump, which happens when multiple disconnected CAD lines are exported as a single polyline. By splitting the polyline at this point, I can eliminate that spurious streak!\n\nI\'m also considering the Defpoints layer. I am ensuring that Defpoints lines never make it into finalEntities by analyzing layer names. The logic considers several variations of \"Defpoint\" in uppercase.\n\nFinally, I\'ve got long construction lines on my radar. I am beginning to explore the `isArtifactStreakSegment` function.\n\n\n**Assessing Diagonal Streaks**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the criteria for identifying diagonal streaks and long orthogonal lines, primarily within the `isArtifactStreakSegment` function. I\'ve uncovered a crucial aspect: the check for lines exceeding 1.5 times the maximum diagonal length. Further, diagonal lines require a specific proportion of both `dx` and `dy` relative to the overall length. I\'m especially interested in the 0.35 threshold when orthogonal lines extend across the interior, and the importance of excluding those on border layers.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_56955"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Improve artifact streak detection and polyline false closure filtering in modelExpander.ts\",\"EndLine\":390,\"Instruction\":\"Update isArtifactStreakSegment and polyline processing in modelExpander.ts\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"  function isArtifactStreakSegment(\\n    p1: Point2D,\\n    p2: Point2D,\\n    layerName: string = \'\'\\n  ): boolean {\\n    const dx = Math.abs(p2.x - p1.x);\\n    const dy = Math.abs(p2.y - p1.y);\\n    const len = Math.hypot(dx, dy);\\n    if (!isFinite(len) || len === 0) return true;\\n    if (len > maxDiag * 1.5) return true;\\n\\n    // Diagonal streak cutting across viewports\\n    const isDiagonal = dx > len * 0.18 && dy > len * 0.18;\\n    if (isDiagonal && len > maxDiag * 0.20) {\\n      return true;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Long horizontal or vertical line cutting through interior\\n    const isOrthogonal = dx < len * 0.02 || dy < len * 0.02;\\n    if (isOrthogonal && len > Math.max(spanW, spanH) * 0.35) {\\n      const lyrUpper = layerName.toUpperCase();\\n      const isBorderLayer =\\n        lyrUpper.includes(\'BORDER\') ||\\n        lyrUpper.includes(\'TITLE\') ||\\n        lyrUpper.includes(\'FRAME\') ||\\n        lyrUpper.includes(\'SHEET\');\\n      if (!isBorderLayer) {\\n        const midX = (p1.x + p2.x) / 2;\\n        const midY = (p1.y + p2.y) / 2;\\n        const nearOuterX =\\n          Math.abs(midX - minX) < spanW * 0.035 ||\\n          Math.abs(midX - maxX) < spanW * 0.035;\\n        const nearOuterY =\\n          Math.abs(midY - minY) < spanH * 0.035 ||\\n          Math.abs(midY - maxY) < spanH * 0.035;\\n        if (!nearOuterX && !nearOuterY) {\\n          return true;\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  const finalEntities: CadEntity[] = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < expanded.length; i++) {\\n    const e = expanded[i];\\n    const lyrUpper = String(e.layer || \'\').toUpperCase();\\n    if (\\n      lyrUpper === \'DEFPOINTS\' ||\\n      lyrUpper.includes(\'DEFPOINT\') ||\\n      lyrUpper === \'NPLT\' ||\\n      lyrUpper.includes(\'NO_PLOT\') ||\\n      lyrUpper.includes(\'NON_PLOT\')\\n    ) {\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n\\n    if (e.type === \'LINE\' && e.start && e.end) {\\n      if (isArtifactStreakSegment(e.start, e.end, e.layer)) continue;\\n      finalEntities.push(e);\\n    } else if (e.type === \'LWPOLYLINE\' && e.vertices && e.vertices.length >= 2) {\\n      // Calculate median segment length in this polyline to detect anomalous jumps\\n      const segLengths: number[] = [];\\n      for (let s = 1; s < Math.min(e.vertices.length, 30); s++) {\\n        segLengths.push(\\n          Math.hypot(\\n            e.vertices[s].x - e.vertices[s - 1].x,\\n            e.vertices[s].y - e.vertices[s - 1].y\\n          )\\n        );\\n      }\\n      segLengths.sort((a, b) => a - b);\\n      const medianStep =\\n        segLengths[Math.floor(segLengths.length / 2)] || 10;\\n\\n      // Check false polyline closure (connecting disparate ends of drawing)\\n      if (e.closed && e.vertices.length >= 3) {\\n        const v0 = e.vertices[0];\\n        const vn = e.vertices[e.vertices.length - 1];\\n        const closeDist = Math.hypot(vn.x - v0.x, vn.y - v0.y);\\n        if (\\n          isArtifactStreakSegment(vn, v0, e.layer) ||\\n          (closeDist > Math.max(medianStep * 8, 80) &&\\n            closeDist > Math.min(spanW, spanH) * 0.12)\\n        ) {\\n          e.closed = false;\\n        }\\n      }\\n\\n      // Filter internal jump streaks in polylines\\n      let currentSubVerts = [e.vertices[0]];\\n      for (let k = 1; k < e.vertices.length; k++) {\\n        const prev = e.vertices[k - 1];\\n        const cur = e.vertices[k];\\n        const segLen = Math.hypot(cur.x - prev.x, cur.y - prev.y);\\n        const isJump =\\n          isArtifactStreakSegment(prev, cur, e.layer) ||\\n          (segLen > Math.max(medianStep * 15, 200) &&\\n            segLen > Math.min(spanW, spanH) * 0.18);\\n\\n        if (isJump) {\\n          if (currentSubVerts.length >= 2) {\\n            finalEntities.push({\\n              id: `${e.id}_sub${k}`,\\n              type: \'LWPOLYLINE\',\\n              layer: e.layer,\\n              aci: e.aci,\\n              linetype: e.linetype,\\n              lineweight: e.lineweight,\\n              closed: false,\\n              vertices: currentSubVerts,\\n            });\\n          }\\n          currentSubVerts = [cur];\\n        } else {\\n          currentSubVerts.push(cur);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      if (currentSubVerts.length >= 2) {\\n        e.vertices = currentSubVerts;\\n        finalEntities.push(e);\\n      }\\n    } else {\\n      finalEntities.push(e);\\n    }\\n  }\",\"StartLine\":335,\"TargetContent\":\"  function isArtifactStreakSegment(p1: Point2D, p2: Point2D): boolean {\\n    const dx = Math.abs(p2.x - p1.x);\\n    const dy = Math.abs(p2.y - p1.y);\\n    const len = Math.hypot(dx, dy);\\n    if (len > maxDiag * 1.5) return true;\\n    const isDiagonal = dx > len * 0.22 && dy > len * 0.22;\\n    if (isDiagonal && len > maxDiag * 0.22) {\\n      return true;\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  const finalEntities: CadEntity[] = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < expanded.length; i++) {\\n    const e = expanded[i];\\n    if (e.type === \'LINE\' && e.start && e.end) {\\n      if (isArtifactStreakSegment(e.start, e.end)) continue;\\n      finalEntities.push(e);\\n    } else if (e.type === \'LWPOLYLINE\' && e.vertices && e.vertices.length >= 2) {\\n      if (e.closed && e.vertices.length >= 3) {\\n        const v0 = e.vertices[0];\\n        const vn = e.vertices[e.vertices.length - 1];\\n        if (isArtifactStreakSegment(vn, v0)) {\\n          e.closed = false;\\n        }\\n      }\\n      let currentSubVerts = [e.vertices[0]];\\n      for (let k = 1; k < e.vertices.length; k++) {\\n        const prev = e.vertices[k - 1];\\n        const cur = e.vertices[k];\\n        if (isArtifactStreakSegment(prev, cur)) {\\n          if (currentSubVerts.length >= 2) {\\n            finalEntities.push({\\n              id: `${e.id}_sub${k}`,\\n              type: \'LWPOLYLINE\',\\n              layer: e.layer,\\n              aci: e.aci,\\n              linetype: e.linetype,\\n              lineweight: e.lineweight,\\n              closed: false,\\n              vertices: currentSubVerts,\\n            });\\n          }\\n          currentSubVerts = [cur];\\n        } else {\\n          currentSubVerts.push(cur);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      if (currentSubVerts.length >= 2) {\\n        e.vertices = currentSubVerts;\\n        finalEntities.push(e);\\n      }\\n    } else {\\n      finalEntities.push(e);\\n    }\\n  }\",\"TargetFile\":\"/src/lib/modelExpander.ts\",\"toolAction\":\"Updating modelExpander streak and polyline filtering\",\"toolSummary\":\"Update modelExpander streak filtering\"}"
