  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Theme Preferences**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating theme preference management within the application\'s core component. My thinking involves importing the `AppThemePreference` type and leveraging `useState` to manage the theme. I\'m exploring how to retrieve the theme from local storage if available, defaulting to a fallback if it\'s not set. This way I have a way to save and restore the user\'s preferred theme.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme Logic**\n\nNow I\'m implementing the logic for theme determination. I\'ve set up `systemDark` with `useState` to track the system\'s dark mode preference, and I\'m also using `useEffect` to listen for system changes, ensuring the app reacts appropriately to system-level theme adjustments. This builds upon my earlier work to fully manage and react to the user\'s selected theme.\n\n\n**Synchronizing Theme Preferences**\n\nI\'ve just finalized the `handleSetThemePreference` callback, which now updates the theme state and attempts to persist the preference in local storage. I\'m also providing user feedback via toasts for theme changes. Finally, I\'m now synchronizing the HTML theme by adjusting `data-ui-theme` attributes and the `dark` class on the `document.documentElement` to reflect the chosen theme, ensuring visual consistency. I\'m still working on passing the theme to `UniversalModeBar`.\n\n\n"
