  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **User Request**: The user provided two side-by-side screenshots of the exact same CAD drawing (`[\354\204\261\354\210\230\352\263\265\354\236\245] \354\203\201\355\222\2102 ...\354\213\244 \354\244\221\353\237\211\354\204\240\353\263\204\352\270\260 \353\217\204\353\251\264`):\n     - `image_51cfee32.png`: The drawing opened in this mobile CAD viewer app.\n     - `image_293c8b98.png`: The exact same drawing opened in desktop AutoCAD.\n   - **The Problems**:\n     1. In the mobile app view (`image_51cfee32.png`), a long white diagonal streak connects the middle conveyor of the top machine down to the yellow control tower on the rightmost machine.\n     2. Several entities visible in AutoCAD are completely missing in the mobile view:\n        - The yellow outer drawing border/title sheet frame (`\353\217\204\353\251\264 \354\231\270\352\263\275 \355\224\204\353\240\210\354\236\204/\354\234\244\352\263\275\354\204\240`) around the entire drawing with grid letters/numbers.\n        - The green dimension lines (`(1214)`, `550`, `350`, `300`, `860\302\26150`, `460`, `125`, `310`, `494`, etc.) and leader arrows (`\342\206\220`, `\342\206\222`).\n   - **Success Criteria**: Identify the root causes of the missing entities and the diagonal streak, and render the drawing identically to AutoCAD desktop.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed**:\n     - System dark mode auto-detection and real-time syncing implemented in `src/App.tsx` and `src/components/UniversalModeBar.tsx`.\n     - Google Drive and Dropbox integrations configured with Google Identity Services (GIS) and Dropbox direct link import.\n     - Invisible and paper space flags handled in `src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts` and `src/lib/dxfParser.ts`.\n   - **Inspected / Root Cause Identified**:\n     - **Cause of Missing Dimensions & Outer Border**:\n       - In `src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts`: For `DIMENSION` entities, `ent.position = { x: 0, y: 0 }` was previously forced, BUT `modelExpander.ts` subtracts `blk.basePoint`. When `blk.basePoint` on `*D...` dimension blocks is non-zero, this shifts dimension entities off into negative space. Dimension blocks in DWG must use their natural insertion point or have basePoint canceled out.\n       - In `src/lib/modelExpander.ts`: The aggressive filter `isArtifactStreakSegment` was filtering any orthogonal line with `len > Math.max(spanW, spanH) * 0.35`. Because the yellow outer border rectangle lines are 100% of `spanW` and `spanH` and slightly inset from the extreme data bounding box, this filter deleted the outer yellow border frame and grid lines.\n       - In `src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts`: `db.entities` was previously completely filtered if `in_paperspace === 1`. But in many AutoCAD DWG drawings (especially Korean factory blueprints like this one), the drawing border frame is drawn in ModelSpace or in block table records `*MODEL_SPACE`.\n     - **Cause of the Diagonal Line**:\n       - Notice in `image_51cfee32.png`: The diagonal line starts at the top machine and ends at the right tower.\n       - In DWG: This is either a `LEADER` / `MULTILEADER` / `DIMENSION` with a leader line whose arrow or landing coordinate was transformed with an inverted OCS or missing vertex, OR an `LWPOLYLINE` that connects across disconnected sub-paths due to an erroneous `closed` flag or vertex parsing in `libreDwgLoader.ts`.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - **Outer Border Frame**: In `modelExpander.ts`, `isArtifactStreakSegment` MUST NOT delete border lines or rectangular loops. Lines on layers like `0`, `TITLE`, `FRAME`, `BORDER`, `SHEET`, `FORM`, `\354\226\221\354\213\235`, `\354\231\270\352\263\275\354\204\240` or lines that form closed rectangular boundaries must never be treated as streaks.\n   - **Dimension Anonymous Blocks (`*D...`)**:\n     - In AutoCAD LibreDWG: A dimension block record (`*D...`) has `b.basePoint` and entities. When an `INSERT` refers to `*D...`, `insPt = raw.insertionPoint || raw.defPoint || { x: 0, y: 0 }`. If `b.basePoint` is set, `tx = ins.x - bp.x`. If `ins` and `bp` are identical, `tx = 0, ty = 0`, keeping the entities at their world coordinates. Forcing `ins = {0,0}` while `bp` was non-zero resulted in `tx = -bp.x`, offsetting all dimensions by 40,000+ units.\n   - **Diagonal Line**:\n     - Check `LEADER` and `LWPOLYLINE` entities. In `libreDwgLoader.ts`:\n       `raw.vertices || raw.points` for `LEADER` often contains arrow point and text attachment point. If text attachment point has WCS/OCS mismatch or `elevation` applied erroneously, it creates a diagonal streak.\n       Also in `modelExpander.ts`: A polyline closing segment connecting vertices across large distances must be removed, BUT legitimate lines must be preserved.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes Across Session**\n   - *Firebase `auth/network-request-failed`*: Caused by iframe / third-party cookie restrictions on Firebase Auth popup. Fixed by adding Google Identity Services (GIS) token client in `googleDrive.ts` and direct share link opener.\n   - *Missing outer border*: Caused by over-aggressive streak segment filtering in `modelExpander.ts`.\n   - *Missing dimension text and lines*: Caused by incorrect `{ x: 0, y: 0 }` override in `libreDwgLoader.ts` colliding with `blk.basePoint` subtraction in `modelExpander.ts`.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Files to modify:\n     - `/src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts`\n     - `/src/lib/modelExpander.ts`\n     - `/src/lib/dxfParser.ts`\n   - Build tools: `compile_applet`, `lint_applet`, `restart_dev_server`.\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. **Fix Dimension Block Handling in `/src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts`**:\n      - For `DIMENSION` blocks (`*D...`), ensure `blk.basePoint` is `{ x: 0, y: 0 }` OR ensure `ent.position` equals `blk.basePoint` so that `ins.x - bp.x = 0`, preserving the dimension\'s true WCS coordinates.\n      - Ensure dimension text (`MTEXT`/`TEXT`) inside dimension blocks is retained and not filtered out.\n   2. **Fix Outer Yellow Frame in `/src/lib/modelExpander.ts`**:\n      - Remove the over-aggressive orthogonal streak filter that deleted the border frame.\n      - Ensure border/frame lines and lines belonging to standard sheet layers are never pruned.\n   3. **Fix Diagonal Streak**:\n      - In `/src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts` and `/src/lib/modelExpander.ts`: Identify diagonal segments in `LEADER` / `LWPOLYLINE` where `dx > 0` and `dy > 0` across different machine blocks (e.g., `len > 2000` connecting distinct clusters) and filter out non-continuous jump segments.\n   4. **Compile & Lint**: Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together, then `restart_dev_server`.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - The output must match the AutoCAD desktop reference (`image_293c8b98.png`): yellow outer title sheet border visible, green dimensions visible, no phantom diagonal line.\n   - Use TypeScript and Tailwind CSS, adhere to React 19 standards.\n</summary>"
