    thinking: "**Analyzing Model Expander**\n\nI\'m currently delving into the `expandList` function within `src/lib/modelExpander.ts`. I\'ve keyed in on the INSERT events and their relationship to block names. I\'m focusing on the conditions under which a block is found and used after an insert. I\'m especially focused on the specific data structure used, and the relationship between blockName and blk.\n\n\n**Examining Edge Cases**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a particular conditional block usage within the `expandList` function, specifically related to dimension entities. I\'m unpacking the logic where block names begin with \"*D\" and exploring the parameters for `isDim`. I\'m also examining the implications of scaling and rotation, and how these transformations affect base points and insertion coordinates to understand the geometric transformations. I\'ve also pivoted to examining the extents percentile and focusing on outliers.\n\n\n**Refining Streak Filtering**\n\nI\'ve been working on refining the artifact streak segment filtering logic. I\'ve removed the orthogonal line deletion and am now only focusing on filtering diagonal streaks, particularly those that span disparate machine views or extend significantly into space. I\'ve updated `isArtifactStreakSegment` function, using this diagonal logic.\n\n\n**Investigating Line Breaks**\n\nI\'m now examining how the line break logic works within polylines. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the criteria used to identify \"jumps\" within polyline segments. I am analyzing the `isArtifactStreakSegment` function and associated distance calculations, especially the thresholds related to `medianStep` and overall segment lengths. I\'m also examining how these jumps lead to the splitting of a polyline into multiple entities.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_207336"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Ensure dimension blocks preserve WCS coordinates in modelExpander\",\"EndLine\":165,\"Instruction\":\"Support dimension blocks with WCS coordinates\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"      if (e.type === \'INSERT\' && e.blockName) {\\n        const blk = findBlock(e.blockName);\\n        if (\\n          blk &&\\n          blk.entities &&\\n          blk.entities.length > 0 &&\\n          !visited.has(blk.name)\\n        ) {\\n          const isDim = blk.name.toUpperCase().startsWith(\'*D\');\\n          const bp = isDim ? { x: 0, y: 0 } : (blk.basePoint || { x: 0, y: 0 });\\n          const ins = isDim ? { x: 0, y: 0 } : (e.position || { x: 0, y: 0 });\\n          const sx = isDim ? 1 : (e.scaleX !== undefined && e.scaleX !== 0 ? e.scaleX : 1);\\n          const sy = isDim ? 1 : (e.scaleY !== undefined && e.scaleY !== 0 ? e.scaleY : 1);\\n          const rad = isDim ? 0 : (((e.rotation || 0) * Math.PI) / 180);\\n          const cosA = Math.cos(rad);\\n          const sinA = Math.sin(rad);\\n          const a = cosA * sx;\\n          const b = sinA * sx;\\n          const c = -sinA * sy;\\n          const d = cosA * sy;\\n          const tx = ins.x - (a * bp.x + c * bp.y);\\n          const ty = ins.y - (b * bp.x + d * bp.y);\",\"StartLine\":137,\"TargetContent\":\"      if (e.type === \'INSERT\' && e.blockName) {\\n        const blk = findBlock(e.blockName);\\n        if (\\n          blk &&\\n          blk.entities &&\\n          blk.entities.length > 0 &&\\n          !visited.has(blk.name)\\n        ) {\\n          const bp = blk.basePoint || { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n          const ins = e.position || { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n          const sx = e.scaleX !== undefined && e.scaleX !== 0 ? e.scaleX : 1;\\n          const sy = e.scaleY !== undefined && e.scaleY !== 0 ? e.scaleY : 1;\\n          const rad = ((e.rotation || 0) * Math.PI) / 180;\\n          const cosA = Math.cos(rad);\\n          const sinA = Math.sin(rad);