    thinking: "**Examining Polyline Rendering**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how polylines are rendered within `CADCanvas.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m analyzing lines 538-550 to understand the iteration through the polyline data and its vertex structure. I\'m exploring how the `batch.polylines` array is processed and the role of the `verts` variable within the loop. The goal is to fully grasp the rendering pipeline for these shapes.\n\n\n**Refining Vertex Validation**\n\nI\'ve identified a potential issue in polyline rendering where non-finite vertex coordinates (NaN, Infinity) could cause `ctx.moveTo` to fail. I\'ve now introduced a safeguard by checking for finite values of both world and screen coordinates before calling `moveTo`. This should prevent rendering errors caused by invalid vertex data. The loop now skips non-finite vertices.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_66393"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Add finite checks to polyline vertices in CADCanvas\",\"EndLine\":551,\"Instruction\":\"Add finite coordinate validation for polyline drawing in CADCanvas\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"        // Polylines\\n        const polys = batch.polylines;\\n        for (let pIdx = 0; pIdx < polys.length; pIdx++) {\\n          const verts = polys[pIdx].vertices;\\n          if (verts.length < 2) continue;\\n          const v0 = verts[0];\\n          if (!isFinite(v0.x) || !isFinite(v0.y)) continue;\\n          const s0 = worldToScreen(v0.x, v0.y);\\n          if (!isFinite(s0.x) || !isFinite(s0.y)) continue;\\n          ctx.moveTo(s0.x, s0.y);\\n          for (let k = 1; k < verts.length; k++) {\\n            const vk = verts[k];\\n            if (!isFinite(vk.x) || !isFinite(vk.y)) continue;\\n            const sk = worldToScreen(vk.x, vk.y);\\n            if (!isFinite(sk.x) || !isFinite(sk.y)) continue;\\n            ctx.lineTo(sk.x, sk.y);\\n          }\\n          if (polys[pIdx].closed) ctx.closePath();\\n        }\",\"StartLine\":537,\"TargetContent\":\"        // Polylines\\n        const polys = batch.polylines;\\n        for (let pIdx = 0; pIdx < polys.length; pIdx++) {\\n          const verts = polys[pIdx].vertices;\\n          if (verts.length < 2) continue;\\n          const v0 = verts[0];\\n          const s0 = worldToScreen(v0.x, v0.y);\\n          ctx.moveTo(s0.x, s0.y);\\n          for (let k = 1; k < verts.length; k++) {\\n            const sk = worldToScreen(verts[k].x, verts[k].y);\\n            ctx.lineTo(sk.x, sk.y);\\n          }\\n          if (polys[pIdx].closed) ctx.closePath();\\n        }\",\"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/CADCanvas.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Editing CADCanvas.tsx\",\"toolSummary\":\"Add finite checks for polyline drawing\"}"
