  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining CAD Processing**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating a preprocessing step into the CAD drawing loaders. The goal is to automatically filter or normalize problematic entities, specifically those with infinite coordinates or excessively small points. This filtering process will address potential issues and ensure more robust data handling within the loaders for `src/lib/dxfParser.ts` and `src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts`.\n\n\n**Implementing Entity Filtering**\n\nI\'m now identifying abnormal geometric entities in the CAD loaders, specifically focusing on lines. The preprocessing step in `src/lib/dxfParser.ts` and `src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts` will filter out lines with infinite or NaN coordinates, and those with nearly zero length (degenerate lines), defined by coordinate checks (`isFinite`, `isNaN`, or `distance < tolerance`). My current focus is to refine the tolerance levels to achieve the best balance between data integrity and performance.\n\n\n"
