  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining CAD Sanitization**\n\nI\'m starting to formalize the rules for a CAD sanitizer. The first function will be `isSaneCoord`, ensuring a value is a finite number, not NaN, and within reasonable bounds, specifically less than 1e7 in absolute value (as coordinates beyond this are unrealistic in millimeter CAD systems). I\'m writing the function definition now, along with its type signature.\n\n\n**Refining Sane Geometry**\n\nI\'ve outlined `sanitizePoint`, which validates and cleans coordinate pairs, along with the criteria for LINE, LWPOLYLINE, and CIRCLE types. A zero-length line and infinite line artifacts are flagged for removal. For LWPOLYLINE, I\'m filtering vertices, deduplicating them, and computing a bounding box to detect degenerated polylines. Very long polyline segments get split. CIRCLE\'s sanitation targets the center point and radius.\n\n\n**Expanding Entity Sanitization**\n\nI\'m now focusing on sanitizing ARC, ELLIPSE, TEXT, and INSERT entities. The radius for ARC must fall between 1e-4 and 1e7, along with sane center coordinates. I\'m normalizing the start and end angles of arcs to be within 0 to 360 degrees. For ELLIPSE, I\'m verifying the center, major axis, and clamping the axis ratio. Text validation includes position, height, and content. INSERT requires position, scaling, and rotation to be within sane bounds. Finally, I will implement entity list and drawing model sanitation to apply these rules. I\'m moving toward `src/lib/cadSanitizer.ts` with `write_to_file`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_120764"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"/**\\n * @license\\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\\n */\\n\\nimport {\\n  CadBlock,\\n  CadEntity,\\n  DrawingModel,\\n  LineEntity,\\n  Point2D,\\n  PolylineEntity,\\n  Vertex2D,\\n} from \'../types/cad\';\\n\\nconst MAX_COORD_ABS = 1e7;\\nconst MIN_GEOM_SPAN = 1e-4; // 0.0001 units: below this is a degenerate microscopic dot\\n\\n/**\\n * Validates whether a numerical coordinate is finite, non-NaN, and within sane CAD boundaries.\\n */\\nexport function isSaneCoord(v: unknown): v is number {\\n  return (\\n    typeof v === \'number\' &&\\n    Number.isFinite(v) &&\\n    !Number.isNaN(v) &&\\n    Math.abs(v) <= MAX_COORD_ABS\\n  );\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Validates a 2D point.\\n */\\nexport function isSanePoint(pt: unknown): pt is Point2D {\\n  if (!pt || typeof pt !== \'object\') return false;\\n  const p = pt as Point2D;\\n  return isSaneCoord(p.x) && isSaneCoord(p.y);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Sanitizes and validates a single CAD entity.\\n * Returns null if the entity is degenerate, microscopic, or has infinite/invalid coordinates.\\n */\\nexport function sanitizeCadEntity(ent: CadEntity | null | undefined): CadEntity | null {\\n  if (!ent || !ent.type) return null;\\n\\n  switch (ent.type) {\\n    case \'LINE\': {\\n      const line = ent as LineEntity;\\n      if (!isSanePoint(line.start) || !isSanePoint(line.end)) return null;\\n\\n      const dx = line.end.x - line.start.x;\\n      const dy = line.end.y - line.start.y;\\n      const len = Math.hypot(dx, dy);\\n\\n      // Filter out zero-length lines / microscopic points\\n      if (!Number.isFinite(len) || len < MIN_GEOM_SPAN) return null;\\n\\n      // Filter out astronomical infinite rays / overflow lines\\n      if (len > MAX_COORD_ABS) return null;\\n\\n      return line;\\n    }\\n\\n    case \'LWPOLYLINE\': {\\n      const poly = ent as PolylineEntity;\\n      if (!Array.isArray(poly.vertices) || poly.vertices.length < 2) return null;\\n\\n      const saneVerts: Vertex2D[] = [];\\n      let minX = Infinity,\\n        minY = Infinity,\\n        maxX = -Infinity,\\n        maxY = -Infinity;\\n\\n      for (let i = 0; i < poly.vertices.length; i++) {\\n        const v = poly.vertices[i];\\n        if (!v || !isSaneCoord(v.x) || !isSaneCoord(v.y)) continue;\\n\\n        // Skip consecutive duplicate vertices (microscopic zero-length segment)\\n        if (saneVerts.length > 0) {\\n          const prev = saneVerts[saneVerts.length - 1];\\n          const dist = Math.hypot(v.x - prev.x, v.y - prev.y);\\n          if (dist < MIN_GEOM_SPAN) {\\n            // Keep bulge if present on the duplicate\\n            if (v.bulge && !prev.bulge) prev.bulge = v.bulge;\\n            continue;\\n          }\\n        }\\n\\n        saneVerts.push({\\n          x: v.x,\\n          y: v.y,\\n          bulge: typeof v.bulge === \'number\' && Number.isFinite(v.bulge) ? v.bulge : undefined,\\n        });\\n\\n        if (v.x < minX) minX = v.x;\\n        if (v.y < minY) minY = v.y;\\n        if (v.x > maxX) maxX = v.x;\\n        if (v.y > maxY) maxY = v.y;\\n      }\\n\\n      if (saneVerts.length < 2) return null;\\n\\n      // Filter out polylines whose total bounding span is microscopic (noise/dots)\\n      const spanW = maxX - minX;\\n      const spanH = maxY - minY;\\n      if (Math.hypot(spanW, spanH) < MIN_GEOM_SPAN) return null;\\n\\n      poly.vertices = saneVerts;\\n      return poly;\\n    }\\n\\n    case \'CIRCLE\': {\\n      if (!isSanePoint(ent.center)) return null;\\n      if (!Number.isFinite(ent.radius) || ent.radius < MIN_GEOM_SPAN || ent.radius > MAX_COORD_ABS) {\\n        return null;\\n      }\\n      return ent;\\n    }\\n\\n    case \'ARC\': {\\n      if (!isSanePoint(ent.center)) return null;\\n      if (!Number.isFinite(ent.radius) || ent.radius < MIN_GEOM_SPAN || ent.radius > MAX_COORD_ABS) {\\n        return null;\\n      }\\n      const sa = Number(ent.startAngle || 0);\\n      const ea = Number(ent.endAngle || 0);\\n      if (!Number.isFinite(sa) || !Number.isFinite(ea)) return null;\\n\\n      // Normalize angles\\n      ent.startAngle = ((sa % 360) + 360) % 360;\\n      ent.endAngle = ((ea % 360) + 360) % 360;\\n\\n      return ent;\\n    }\\n\\n    case \'ELLIPSE\': {\\n      if (!isSanePoint(ent.center) || !isSanePoint(ent.majorAxis)) return null;\\n      const majLen = Math.hypot(ent.majorAxis.x, ent.majorAxis.y);\\n      if (!Number.isFinite(majLen) || majLen < MIN_GEOM_SPAN || majLen > MAX_COORD_ABS) {\\n        return null;\\n      }\\n      let ratio = Number(ent.axisRatio || 0.5);\\n      if (!Number.isFinite(ratio) || ratio <= 0) ratio = 0.5;\\n      if (ratio > 1) ratio = 1;\\n      ent.axisRatio = ratio;\\n      return ent;\\n    }\\n\\n    case \'TEXT\': {\\n      if (!isSanePoint(ent.position)) return null;\\n      let h = Number(ent.height || 0);\\n      if (!Number.isFinite(h) || h < MIN_GEOM_SPAN || h > MAX_COORD_ABS) {\\n        h = 10;\\n      }\\n      ent.height = h;\\n      if (!Number.isFinite(ent.rotation)) ent.rotation = 0;\\n      if (!ent.text || typeof ent.text !== \'string\' || !ent.text.trim()) return null;\\n      return ent;\\n    }\\n\\n    case \'INSERT\': {\\n      if (!isSanePoint(ent.position)) return null;\\n      if (!ent.blockName || typeof ent.blockName !== \'string\') return null;\\n\\n      let sx = Number(ent.scaleX !== undefined ? ent.scaleX : 1);\\n      let sy = Number(ent.scaleY !== undefined ? ent.scaleY : 1);\\n      if (!Number.isFinite(sx) || Math.abs(sx) < 1e-7 || Math.abs(sx) > 1e6) sx = 1;\\n      if (!Number.isFinite(sy) || Math.abs(sy) < 1e-7 || Math.abs(sy) > 1e6) sy = 1;\\n      ent.scaleX = sx;\\n      ent.scaleY = sy;\\n      if (!Number.isFinite(ent.rotation)) ent.rotation = 0;\\n      return ent;\\n    }\\n\\n    case \'RASTER_PREVIEW\': {\\n      return ent;\\n    }\\n\\n    default:\\n      return null;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Sanitizes an array of entities, removing microscopic or invalid items.\\n */\\nexport function sanitizeEntityList(list: CadEntity[]): CadEntity[] {\\n  if (!Array.isArray(list)) return [];\\n  const result: CadEntity[] = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\\n    const s = sanitizeCadEntity(list[i]);\\n    if (s) result.push(s);\\n  }\\n  return result;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Preprocesses and sanitizes a complete DrawingModel, cleaning both top-level entities and block definitions.\\n */\\nexport function sanitizeDrawingModel(model: DrawingModel): DrawingModel {\\n  if (!model) return model;\\n\\n  // Sanitize top-level entities\\n  const cleanEntities = sanitizeEntityList(model.entities || []);\\n\\n  // Sanitize all block entities and base points\\n  const cleanBlocks: Record<string, CadBlock> = {};\\n  if (model.blocks) {\\n    Object.keys(model.blocks).forEach((k) => {\\n      const b = model.blocks[k];\\n      if (!b) return;\\n      const bp = isSanePoint(b.basePoint) ? b.basePoint : { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n      cleanBlocks[k] = {\\n        name: b.name || k,\\n        basePoint: bp,\\n        entities: sanitizeEntityList(b.entities || []),\\n      };\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    ...model,\\n    blocks: cleanBlocks,\\n    entities: cleanEntities,\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"Description\":\"Create CAD geometric sanitizer module to filter infinite coordinates, abnormal leaps, and microscopic degenerate entities\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/lib/cadSanitizer.ts\",\"toolAction\":\"Creating cadSanitizer.ts\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create CAD geometric sanitizer module\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\357\027\n\354\027\001i\024}\023_`?_O\342\227\342\253\017\315\332\203\325w\372\021\337\030-B\327-]\307\275\371\321o\204b5\362\365U\235\304\034\346\316\036\264\325p<\250K\376\177\217\347\273TX\034D\244\237\r\021\354.\317~\203\373Z\021a*\334\224\000\v\324n~\250\323\a\336\f\345\313g\211\276\005\305\313\f\317e\212i\332q\021\\m\000W\237d\375\2213e/;\257\311\342\242%\307\342\357:4\274E\326u\340\212\252\266D\345^\203D\255\333\251\255XD\022=\001\005\024\255\372xCH6\271\037\353\373\315q&\036\212\367\227\300q\346\3228;\232\250\003\"\355\203\003\231\223\006\276\'\343\316\311\021\307\236\367&\2507\003\001cD\270\302g\v\0041\203\253\370\257\217\006\355\030\\\3002\341z\367v/O\227\216\330Y\340\330\204\336[\372\360<\277V\275\237\255\247\v\255Z\317\027\0228\333\370\031\017e\312\367D\377\240\312\017\037\314\237\257Y7\365My\361J\276\002\336\272\030\316\262#7v\025\nT\023\353/\323S\344\2576\225\204\244\027\373\306\242.\234\004\021\340\266\3138\354\243i=\363cU\333^\205&?l\250\353g\213\277AQ\350\362Zn\307{R\372d^\314\036\035W\312\204=\202$\203.\262_\213N\031s\257\260\306\362?\272c\256\"\342\017\374\262\341i\003\355O&\364#\326xr\263C\254\200\3056.[]\261\274\214\310 \223\373\223F@\213\307\225\317\353~\304\322u)\351\366\214\231\253\216G\243\266\207U\205\326z\343\0255f\347C\367\a\n\r3+?\270{\376\\!B \v\211\370\b/\376\000\004\331\267#\002\032*&\252\361\334\333%\200u,\377\306\276\365\307EA\346\226\254\000\363\231\351\216\241\254\025g\336\263a,\024\374?\')\316\336\264\234\b<\314\270\367\252\275\305\3061%_\016\354\321\272t\346\311\214K(3R\\G\302\351\247\\\376\'\222\250\274\335#\250j\366\2103\301\361H{\227\371\263G$\347eu\307\325\3524jN\205\276\276l\226\035\347\232\032\336ai\357\037\024\265[\023\231\204\276\30556\201\022\246\214\341\vi\342\221\034v\326L\360\231\352M\225\317-p\314nK\254\342_C\003\2677\265\375\356\v\246;\364D?\330z\232z)\035\016$\307\230\344\005!\225\260\224,u\253$M\275&W\342@\330\371\336\301s\246\270x\177|\322\1771\300\324o\263)d\030\362n\002D\321\275\