  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Canvas Refs**\n\nI\'m currently working in `CADCanvas.tsx` at line 401. I\'ve added `offscreenRef` and `animFrameRef` to the code, both using `useRef`. These should help manage canvas elements and animation frames. Also, the `latestRef` is being configured.\n\n\n**Refining Rendering Logic**\n\nI\'ve just added camera parameters, like `camX`, `camY`, `zoom`, and `rotation` to the `latestRef`, ensuring the most up-to-date values are readily available. I\'ve also implemented atomic blitting in the render function to get a flicker-free display. I\'m focusing on ensuring smooth offscreen rendering and a responsive user interface now.\n\n\n**Implementing Animation Frames**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating `requestAnimationFrame` and `cancelAnimationFrame` within the rendering cycle to optimize updates. I\'m ensuring smooth animation transitions by managing the `animFrameRef` to avoid unnecessary re-renders. Also, I\'m incorporating the `latestRef` in event listeners (line 838-1020) for consistent camera state access.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_152119"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Add offscreen double-buffering and rAF to render loop in CADCanvas\",\"EndLine\":425,\"Instruction\":\"Add offscreen buffer and alias ctx = drawCtx in render\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"  const offscreenRef = useRef<HTMLCanvasElement | null>(null);\\n  const animFrameRef = useRef<number | null>(null);\\n\\n  const latestRef = useRef({\\n    camX,\\n    camY,\\n    zoom,\\n    rotation,\\n    mode,\\n    unitScaleFactor,\\n    screenToWorld,\\n    findSnapPoint,\\n    onUpdateCamera,\\n    onUpdateMouseWorld,\\n    handlePointTap,\\n  });\\n\\n  latestRef.current = {\\n    camX,\\n    camY,\\n    zoom,\\n    rotation,\\n    mode,\\n    unitScaleFactor,\\n    screenToWorld,\\n    findSnapPoint,\\n    onUpdateCamera,\\n    onUpdateMouseWorld,\\n    handlePointTap,\\n  };\\n\\n  // Double-Buffered 60FPS Render Loop (100% Flicker-Free)\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n    if (!canvas) return;\\n\\n    const render = () => {\\n      const cw = canvas.width;\\n      const ch = canvas.height;\\n      if (!cw || !ch) return;\\n\\n      let offscreen = offscreenRef.current;\\n      if (!offscreen) {\\n        offscreen = document.createElement(\'canvas\');\\n        offscreenRef.current = offscreen;\\n      }\\n      if (offscreen.width !== cw || offscreen.height !== ch) {\\n        offscreen.width = cw;\\n        offscreen.height = ch;\\n      }\\n      const drawCtx = offscreen.getContext(\'2d\', { alpha: false });\\n      if (!drawCtx) return;\\n      const ctx = drawCtx;\\n\\n      // Surface Background: AI-Vault Soft Ivory vs Dark vs Blueprint\\n      const bgMap = { white: \'#F8F7F4\', dark: \'#0B101B\', blueprint: \'#071B38\' };\\n      ctx.fillStyle = bgMap[theme] || \'#F8F7F4\';\\n      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, cw, ch);\",\"StartLine\":401,\"TargetContent\":\"  // 60FPS Render Loop\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n    if (!canvas) return;\\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext(\'2d\', { alpha: false });\\n    if (!ctx) return;\\n\\n    let animId: number;\\n    const render = () => {\\n      const cw = canvas.width;\\n      const ch = canvas.height;\\n      if (!cw || !ch) return;\\n\\n      // Surface Background: AI-Vault Soft Ivory vs Dark vs Blueprint\\n      const bgMap = { white: \'#F8F7F4\', dark: \'#0B101B\', blueprint: \'#071B38\' };\\n      ctx.fillStyle = bgMap[theme] || \'#F8F7F4\';\\n      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, cw, ch);\",\"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/CADCanvas.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Editing CADCanvas.tsx\",\"toolSummary\":\"Add double-buffered canvas in CADCanvas\"}"
