  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **User Request**: \"\354\247\200\352\270\210 \353\217\204\353\251\264 \353\266\200\353\245\270 \355\231\224\353\251\264\354\227\220\354\204\234 \355\231\224\353\251\264\354\235\264\353\217\231\355\225\240\353\225\214 \354\227\204\354\262\255 \353\271\240\353\245\270 \352\271\234\353\271\241\352\261\260\353\246\274\354\235\264 \353\260\234\354\203\235\355\225\264\" (When panning/moving the screen after opening the drawing, very fast flickering occurs).\n   - **Success Criteria**: Completely eliminate the fast flickering during pan/drag/touch moves while preserving smooth 60fps pan/zoom performance, accurate coordinate tracking, and correct CAD rendering.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed in earlier turns**:\n     - Created `src/lib/cadSanitizer.ts`: Preprocessing pipeline filtering infinite coordinates (`Math.abs(v) > 1e7`), degenerate zero-length lines/dots (`< 1e-4`), and abnormal leap segments.\n     - Integrated `cadSanitizer.ts` into `src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts` and `src/lib/dxfParser.ts`.\n     - Verified and compiled cleanly with `compile_applet` and `lint_applet`.\n   - **Root Cause of Flickering Identified**:\n     1. In `src/components/CADCanvas.tsx`, the onscreen canvas (`{ alpha: false }`) was cleared directly with `ctx.fillRect(0, 0, cw, ch)` synchronously on every React state change without double buffering. Because complex CAD drawings execute tens of thousands of path operations, the browser compositor thread paints the canvas between `ctx.fillRect` and the finished strokes, causing rapid alternate-frame flashing (blank frame -> drawn frame -> blank frame).\n     2. In `src/components/CADCanvas.tsx`, `render()` was executed synchronously in `useEffect` on every single pixel of mouse/touch movement instead of being throttled/coalesced with `requestAnimationFrame`.\n     3. On every pixel of `onMouseMove`, `onUpdateMouseWorld(wPt)` was called, updating `mouseWorld` in `App.tsx` and triggering redundant top-level re-renders on top of `onUpdateCamera`.\n     4. The interaction listener `useEffect` (lines 898-1020 in `CADCanvas.tsx`) had `[camX, camY, zoom, ...]` in its dependency array, causing all 6 event listeners (`mousedown`, `mousemove`, `mouseup`, `wheel`, `touchstart`, `touchmove`, `touchend`) to be unmounted and re-mounted on `window` and `canvas` on every single pixel moved.\n   - **Partially Completed Edits in `src/components/CADCanvas.tsx`**:\n     - Added `offscreenRef`, `animFrameRef`, and `latestRef` declarations around line 400.\n     - Updated start of `render()` to draw into `offscreenCanvas` via `const ctx = drawCtx`.\n     - Added atomic blit `onScreenCtx.drawImage(offscreen, 0, 0)` and `requestAnimationFrame` scheduling in lines 780-805.\n   - **Remaining to Update in `src/components/CADCanvas.tsx`**:\n     - Update mouse and touch listeners (`onMouseDown`, `onMouseMove`, `onMouseUp`, `onWheel`, `onTouchStart`, `onTouchMove`, `onTouchEnd`) to use `latestRef.current`.\n     - In `onMouseMove`, do NOT call `onUpdateMouseWorld` during active panning (`isDraggingRef.current && mode === \'pan\'`); only update `onUpdateMouseWorld` when hovering or when drag ends.\n     - Change the interaction listener `useEffect` dependency array to `[]` so listeners mount once and do not thrash on every frame.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - In HTML5 2D Canvas rendering, calling `ctx.fillRect` on an onscreen canvas while tens of thousands of vector lines are drawn synchronously causes severe compositor tearing/flickering.\n   - Using an in-memory `offscreen` canvas buffer with a single final `onScreenCtx.drawImage(offscreen, 0, 0)` provides true double-buffering and 100% flicker-free rendering.\n   - `requestAnimationFrame` coalesces multiple high-frequency touchmove/mousemove events per VSYNC tick, preventing thread starvation.\n   - Storing reactive props in `latestRef` decouples high-frequency mouse/touch event listeners from React re-renders.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - *Previous Syntax Error in `src/lib/dxfParser.ts`*: Line 13 had missing closing brace `} from \'../types/cad\';`. Fixed and verified with `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` (exit code 0).\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Active file: `/src/components/CADCanvas.tsx`\n   - Build tools: `compile_applet`, `lint_applet`, `restart_dev_server`.\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. **Edit `/src/components/CADCanvas.tsx` lines 910 to 1030**:\n      - Replace direct closures with `latestRef.current`:\n        - In `onMouseDown`: `dragStartCamRef.current = { x: latestRef.current.camX, y: latestRef.current.camY };`\n        - In `onMouseMove`: read `{ camX, camY, zoom, rotation, mode, onUpdateCamera, onUpdateMouseWorld, findSnapPoint, screenToWorld }` from `latestRef.current`. If `isDraggingRef.current && mode === \'pan\'`, update camera and skip `onUpdateMouseWorld`; otherwise update mouse world.\n        - In `onMouseUp`: on drag end, update mouse world once.\n        - In `onWheel`: read `camX, camY, zoom, onUpdateCamera, screenToWorld` from `latestRef.current`.\n        - In `onTouchStart`: `dragStartCamRef.current = { x: latestRef.current.camX, y: latestRef.current.camY };`\n        - In `onTouchMove`: read camera and mode from `latestRef.current`.\n        - In `onTouchEnd`: handle point tap using `latestRef.current.handlePointTap`.\n      - Change the listener `useEffect` dependency array from `[camX, camY, zoom, rotation, mode, findSnapPoint, screenToWorld, onUpdateCamera, onUpdateMouseWorld]` to `[]`.\n   2. **Verify Build**:\n      - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together in one turn.\n      - Call `restart_dev_server`.\n   3. **Respond to User**:\n      - Provide a concise explanation of the double-buffering, rAF coalescing, and event listener stability fixes implemented to eliminate screen flickering.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Maintain React 19 and Tailwind CSS standards.\n   - No mock fallbacks.\n   - Ensure touch gesture support on mobile devices remains responsive and accurate.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 324
    included_step_index_end: 549
