  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Mouse Interaction**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `UniversalModeBar` component and how it interacts with mouse input. Specifically, I\'m focusing on lines 593-595, and the `mouseWorld` prop passed to the rendering. The `onUpdateMouseWorld` function, called on every mouse or touch movement, triggers a `setMouseWorld` state update, causing a full re-render of the `App` component. This could have performance implications, especially with complex CAD views.\n\n\n**Refining Pan Interaction**\n\nI\'m now investigating the double state updates triggered during panning: `onUpdateCamera` and `onUpdateMouseWorld`. I\'ve identified that every pixel of panning was causing both of these state updates in the `App` component. Further examination of `CADCanvas.tsx` revealed an asynchronous clearing issue in the canvas due to double-buffering. I\'m focusing on lines 900-1080 of `CADCanvas.tsx` to optimize input event handling for improved performance during pan operations, specifically aiming to skip redundant `onUpdateMouseWorld` calls during active panning.\n\n\n"
