  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Re-renders**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how `App.tsx` re-renders trigger updates in `CADCanvas`, specifically its `useEffect` hook. I\'m examining how changes in `mouseWorld` during hovering or other state updates in `App` \342\200\223 such as the timer, toast messages, toolbar state, or theme preference \342\200\223 influence the canvas\'s refresh cycle. I\'m noting the interplay.\n\n\n**Defining \"Render on Demand\"**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"render on demand\" concept. Instead of constant re-rendering or reacting solely to parent updates, the CADCanvas will only update when a visual change happens, or a `requestRender()` call occurs. This requires identifying what constitutes a visual change. I am currently listing the factors, like camera parameters, theme, grid visibility, model data, selections, measurements, dimensions, and text, that determine when the canvas needs a refresh.\n\n\n"
