  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Render Loop**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on the double-buffered 60FPS render loop within `CADCanvas.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m examining the `useEffect` hook and the logic surrounding the `canvasRef.current` element, to ensure a flicker-free rendering process. I\'m reviewing lines 436 to 806.\n\n\n**Investigating Dependency Array**\n\nI\'ve been looking deeper into the `useEffect` hook\'s dependency array in `CADCanvas.tsx`. The array seems extensive, which is not unusual for a render loop. I see that `screenToWorld` and `worldToScreen` are both dependent on `camX`, `camY`, `zoom`, and `rotation`. The key part is that `snapPointRef.current` can change when in mouse movement, which then invalidates the caches used for screen and world transforms, which invalidates the `useEffect`.\n\n\n**Implementing Request-on-Demand**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on implementing the \"request-on-demand\" rendering technique. I\'m focusing on incorporating a `isDirtyRef` variable and a stable `requestRender()` function. The core idea is to prevent unnecessary redrawing, and I\'m looking at ways to determine and track what requires an update, such as camera changes or other visual updates within the CAD environment.\n\n\n**Caching Render States**\n\nI\'m now implementing state caching to optimize the render loop. My current plan is to skip redrawing if the visual parameters like camera position, entities, dimensions, theme, layers, and measurements haven\'t changed since the last rendered frame. I will be storing the `lastRenderedStateRef` to track these parameters, and then compare the new parameters with the previous state to see if there is any change.\n\n\n**Optimizing Visual Comparisons**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on optimizing visual comparisons. Before executing draw calls, I\'m now comparing the current state against `lastRenderedStateRef.current` to determine if a redraw is necessary. If everything matches, I\'ll return immediately, skipping the render process entirely. I also plan to make the `requestRender()` method explicit.\n\n\n"
