  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing the Render Loop**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the double-buffered 60FPS render loop within the `useEffect` hook. I\'m reviewing the implementation, particularly the use of `canvasRef` and the overall structure, to ensure a flicker-free rendering experience. The focus is on optimization.\n\n\n**Refactoring the Rendering**\n\nI\'m now diving into the proposed refactoring. I intend to convert the `render` function into a `useCallback` to optimize the render loop. I\'m focusing on lines 405-465, which contain the `RenderStateSnapshot` interface and associated refs. This will involve dirty-checking logic within a reactive `useEffect` block, and setting a `requestRender` function. The goal is to improve the efficiency and responsiveness of the rendering process.\n\n\n**Analyzing Data Synchronization**\n\nI\'m now investigating how to synchronize data effectively between `latestRef.current` and the rendering function, specifically lines 467-510. The goal is to ensure the render loop uses the most up-to-date data without unnecessary re-renders. I\'m focusing on the `useEffect` hook and the associated dependencies to optimize the data update mechanism. The use of `requestRender` is key.\n\n\n**Optimizing the Canvas**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the canvas rendering function. I\'m carefully reviewing the logic to ensure that only necessary updates trigger re-renders. I\'m focusing on the data flow from `latestRef.current` to the `render` function to minimize potential performance bottlenecks. The goal is to ensure smooth and responsive rendering.\n\n\n**Evaluating State Comparisons**\n\nI\'m now focusing on efficiently comparing the current render state with the last render state to optimize re-renders. I\'m carefully examining the logic comparing various properties like canvas dimensions, camera position, zoom, rotation, and theme. I\'m also ensuring the correct checking of the length of the entities, batches, texts, rasters, and measurement arrays to minimize unnecessary updates. The goal is to maximize performance by minimizing redrawing.\n\n\n**Implementing Conditional Rendering**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing conditional rendering based on visual changes, and am analyzing the logic surrounding `hasVisualChanges`. I\'ve implemented a mechanism to bypass redraws entirely when there are zero visual changes between frames, which significantly boosts performance. I\'m also now storing the `lastRenderStateRef.current` which holds a `RenderStateSnapshot` with various fields. The goal is to maximize performance by minimizing redrawing.\n\n\n**Examining the Context**\n\nI\'m now investigating the canvas context setup, specifically the use of `getContext(\'2d\', { alpha: false })`. I\'m also looking into the background color application based on the theme. The double-buffered copy from the offscreen canvas to the visible canvas is also under review. I\'m ensuring there are no hidden performance bottlenecks.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_5571854571502706536"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Declare RenderStateSnapshot, dirty flag, latestRef, and start of request-on-demand render function\", \"EndLine\":465, \"Instruction\":\"Replace latestRef and useEffect wrapper with RenderStateSnapshot, dirty checking, and render function declaration\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"  interface RenderStateSnapshot {\\n    cw: number;\\n    ch: number;\\n    camX: number;\\n    camY: number;\\n    zoom: number;\\n    rotation: number;\\n    theme: string;\\n    showGrid: boolean;\\n    enableOsnap: boolean;\\n    textScale: number;\\n    snapKey: string;\\n    entitiesLen: number;\\n    batchesLen: number;\\n    textsLen: number;\\n    rastersLen: number;\\n    layersKey: string;\\n    selectedId: string;\\n    measurementsLen: number;\\n    measurePointsKey: string;\\n  }\\n\\n  const offscreenRef = useRef<HTMLCanvasElement | null>(null);\\n  const animFrameRef = useRef<number | null>(null);\\n  const isDirtyRef = useRef<boolean>(true);\\n  const lastRenderStateRef = useRef<RenderStateSnapshot | null>(null);\\n\\n  const latestRef = useRef({\\n    camX,\\n    camY,\\n    zoom,\\n    rotation,\\n    mode,\\n    unitScaleFactor,\\n    screenToWorld,\\n    worldToScreen,\\n    findSnapPoint,\\n    onUpdateCamera,\\n    onUpdateMouseWorld,\\n    handlePointTap,\\n    updateTouchLoupe,\\n    theme,\\n    showGrid,\\n    enableOsnap,\\n    textScale,\\n    entities,\\n    renderBatches,\\n    textEntities,\\n    rasterEntities,\\n    layers,\\n    selectedEntity,\\n    measurements,\\n    measurePoints,\\n    requestRender: (_force?: boolean) => {},\\n    ensureRendered: () => {},\\n  });\\n\\n  latestRef.current = {\\n    camX,\\n    camY,\\n    zoom,\\n    rotation,\\n    mode,\\n    unitScaleFactor,\\n    screenToWorld,\\n    worldToScreen,\\n    findSnapPoint,\\n    onUpdateCamera,\\n    onUpdateMouseWorld,\\n    handlePointTap,\\n    updateTouchLoupe,\\n    theme,\\n    showGrid,\\n    enableOsnap,\\n    textScale,\\n    entities,\\n    renderBatches,\\n    textEntities,\\n    rasterEntities,\\n    layers,\\n    selectedEntity,\\n    measurements,\\n    measurePoints,\\n    requestRender: (force?: boolean) => {\\n      requestRender(force);\\n    },\\n    ensureRendered: () => {\\n      render();\\n    },\\n  };\\n\\n  // Request-on-Demand Double-Buffered Render Function (Only draws when visual changes occur)\\n  const render = useCallback(() => {\\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n    if (!canvas) return;\\n\\n    const cw = canvas.width;\\n    const ch = canvas.height;\\n    if (!cw || !ch) return;\\n\\n    const {\\n      camX,\\n      camY,\\n      zoom,\\n      rotation,\\n      theme,\\n      showGrid,\\n      enableOsnap,\\n      textScale,\\n      entities,\\n      renderBatches,\\n      textEntities,\\n      rasterEntities,\\n      layers,\\n      selectedEntity,\\n      measurements,\\n      measurePoints,\\n      worldToScreen,\\n      screenToWorld,\\n    } = latestRef.current;\\n\\n    // Check snap point\\n    const curSnap = snapPointRef.current;\\n    const snapKey = curSnap ? `${curSnap.x.toFixed(1)},${curSnap.y.toFixed(1)},${curSnap.type}` : \'\';\\n\\n    // Quick layer visibility signature\\n    let layersKey = \'\';\\n    const layerNames = Object.keys(layers);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < layerNames.length; i++) {\\n      const k = layerNames[i];\\n      layersKey += `${k}:${layers[k]?.visible ? 1 : 0},`;\\n    }\\n\\n    const selectedId = selectedEntity ? `${selectedEntity.type}_${selectedEntity.id || \'\'}` : \'\';\\n    const measurePointsKey = measurePoints.map((p) => `${p.x.toFixed(1)},${p.y.toFixed(1)}`).join(\';\');\\n\\n    const last = lastRenderStateRef.current;\\n    const hasVisualChanges =\\n      isDirtyRef.current ||\\n      !last ||\\n      last.cw !== cw ||\\n      last.ch !== ch ||\\n      last.camX !== camX ||\\n      last.camY !== camY ||\\n      last.zoom !== zoom ||\\n      last.rotation !== rotation ||\\n      last.theme !== theme ||\\n      last.showGrid !== showGrid ||\\n      last.enableOsnap !== enableOsnap ||\\n      last.textScale !== textScale ||\\n      last.snapKey !== snapKey ||\\n      last.entitiesLen !== entities.length ||\\n      last.batchesLen !== renderBatches.length ||\\n      last.textsLen !== textEntities.length ||\\n      last.rastersLen !== rasterEntities.length ||\\n      last.layersKey !== layersKey ||\\n      last.selectedId !== selectedId ||\\n      last.measurementsLen !== measurements.length ||\\n      last.measurePointsKey !== measurePointsKey;\\n\\n    if (!hasVisualChanges) {\\n      // Request-on-demand: Zero visual changes between frames, bypass redraw completely!\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Mark state as clean and record snapshot\\n    isDirtyRef.current = false;\\n    lastRenderStateRef.current = {\\n      cw,\\n      ch,\\n      camX,\\n      camY,\\n      zoom,\\n      rotation,\\n      theme,\\n      showGrid,\\n      enableOsnap,\\n      textScale,\\n      snapKey,\\n      entitiesLen: entities.length,\\n      batchesLen: renderBatches.length,\\n      textsLen: textEntities.length,\\n      rastersLen: rasterEntities.length,\\n      layersKey,\\n      selectedId,\\n      measurementsLen: measurements.length,\\n      measurePointsKey,\\n    };\\n\\n    let offscreen = offscreenRef.current;\\n    if (!offscreen) {\\n      offscreen = document.createElement(\'canvas\');\\n      offscreenRef.current = offscreen;\\n    }\\n    if (offscreen.width !== cw || offscreen.height !== ch) {\\n      offscreen.width = cw;\\n      offscreen.height = ch;\\n    }\\n    const drawCtx = offscreen.getContext(\'2d\', { alpha: false });\\n    if (!drawCtx) return;\\n    const ctx = drawCtx;\\n\\n    // Surface Background: AI-Vault Soft Ivory vs Dark vs Blueprint\\n    const bgMap = { white: \'#F8F7F4\', dark: \'#0B101B\', blueprint: \'#071B38\' };\\n    ctx.fillStyle = bgMap[theme] || \'#F8F7F4\';\\n    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, cw, ch);\", \"StartLine\":404, \"TargetContent\":\"  const offscreenRef = useRef<HTMLCanvasElement | null>(null);\\n  const animFrameRef = useRef<number | null>(null);\\n\\n  const latestRef = useRef({\\n    camX,\\n    camY,\\n    zoom,\\n    rotation,\\n    mode,\\n    unitScaleFactor,\\n    screenToWorld,\\n    findSnapPoint,\\n    onUpdateCamera,\\n    onUpdateMouseWorld,\\n    handlePointTap,\\n    updateTouchLoupe,\\n  });\\n\\n  latestRef.current = {\\n    camX,\\n    camY,\\n    zoom,\\n    rotation,\\n    mode,\\n    unitScaleFactor,\\n    screenToWorld,\\n    findSnapPoint,\\n    onUpdateCamera,\\n    onUpdateMouseWorld,\\n    handlePointTap,\\n    updateTouchLoupe,\\n  };\\n\\n  // Double-Buffered 60FPS Render Loop (100% Flicker-Free)\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n    if (!canvas) return;\\n\\n    const render = () => {\\n      const cw = canvas.width;\\n      const ch = canvas.height;\\n      if (!cw || !ch) return;\\n\\n      let offscreen = offscreenRef.current;\\n      if (!offscreen) {\\n        offscreen = document.createElement(\'canvas\');\\n        offscreenRef.current = offscreen;\\n      }\\n      if (offscreen.width !== cw || offscreen.height !== ch) {\\n        offscreen.width = cw;\\n        offscreen.height = ch;\\n      }\\n      const drawCtx = offscreen.getContext(\'2d\', { alpha: false });\\n      if (!drawCtx) return;\\n      const ctx = drawCtx;\\n\\n      // Surface Background: AI-Vault Soft Ivory vs Dark vs Blueprint\\n      const bgMap = { white: \'#F8F7F4\', dark: \'#0B101B\', blueprint: \'#071B38\' };\\n      ctx.fillStyle = bgMap[theme] || \'#F8F7F4\';\\n      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, cw, ch);\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/CADCanvas.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating render function start\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add dirty check and snapshot to render start\"}"
