  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Pan Behavior**\n\nI\'ve been examining the panning interaction within `CADCanvas.tsx`, specifically the conditions under which the dragging action is triggered and executed. The code snippet highlights how the screen coordinates are used to calculate the pan offset, `dx` and `dy`, when the `pan` mode is active, which should be very informative. I\'m focusing on the delta calculation between the current screen position and the starting screen position for a more precise understanding.\n\n\n**Deconstructing Panning Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implications of `onUpdateCamera`\'s frequent calls triggered by mouse movements. It seems this function, fired repeatedly, directly updates the camera\'s position through prop updates. Specifically, `CADCanvas` re-renders and updates its state with the new camera coordinates as props with each change. The useEffect hook within CADCanvas kicks in with each change.\n\n\n"
