NE`, so I\'m investigating lines 375-436 of `modelExpander.ts`.\n\n\n**Deciphering Polyline Behavior**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how polylines are handled, specifically lines 472-487 in `modelExpander.ts`. I\'m examining conditions related to closing polylines, looking at the distance between the start and end vertices and comparing these values to a threshold dependent on dimensions of the polyline. I also have to consider the filtering logic for internal jump streaks within polylines.\n\n\n**Tracing Polyline Processing**\n\nI\'m now investigating `CADCanvas.tsx`, specifically the handling of polylines within the canvas rendering, lines 730-747. I\'m focusing on how the vertices are processed and rendered on the screen, particularly the world-to-screen coordinate transformation. The code checks for valid coordinates before rendering, so it could filter some data, but I\'m not sure how this influences what polylines might be skipped.\n\n\n"
