  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing DXF Structure**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specifics within the `dxfParser.ts` file, particularly how it handles different entities. I\'ve noted that `SPLINE` entities utilize group codes 10/20 for control points, and 11/21 for fit points. The codes 12/22 and 13/23 are also significant, as they specify start and end tangent direction vectors. Furthermore, I\'ve confirmed that `SOLID` and `TRACE` entities share this usage of codes 10/20, 11/21, and 12/22.\n\n\n**Clarifying Vertex Roles**\n\nI\'m now completely clear on how vertices are handled in DXF files. Specifically, with `SOLID` and `TRACE` entities, the codes 10 through 13 represent the four corner points. Conversely, in `SPLINE` entities, code groups 10 and 20 define control points, and 11 and 21 define fit points. Code groups 12 and 22, and 13 and 23, specify tangent vectors. I am separating `fitPoints` and `controlPoints`, and will avoid interpreting tangent vectors as coordinates.\n\n\n"
