  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Resetting Variables**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the effect\'s dependencies and a significant issue: `prevW` and `prevH` were resetting to zero on every render, which explains the observed behavior. I\'ve confirmed that the effect runs with changes to `entities.length`, `extents`, and `onUpdateCamera`, and also responds to the `window.visualViewport`\'s resize event.\n\n\n**Addressing the Touch Scroll**\n\nI realized that unconditionally setting `canvas.width` and `canvas.height` was causing the canvas to blank out during touch scroll interactions, due to clearing the buffer. To fix this, I\'m refactoring `handleResize` with a `canvasSizeRef`, updating the canvas dimensions and triggering a render only when necessary. This should address the undesired canvas clears and maintain the visual fidelity during touch-based interactions.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_15768341559421300269"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Fix resize observer effect to eliminate canvas clearing and flickering during movement\", \"EndLine\":1061, \"Instruction\":\"Update resize observer to use persistent canvasSizeRef and empty dependency array\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"  // Persistent size tracker to prevent redundant canvas.width buffer resets (which causes blank flicker)\\n  const canvasSizeRef = useRef({ width: 0, height: 0 });\\n\\n  // Window & Container resize observer with orientation auto-adjustment (Mounted once, 100% flicker-free)\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const container = containerRef.current;\\n    if (!container) return;\\n\\n    const handleResize = () => {\\n      const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n      if (!container || !canvas) return;\\n      const rect = container.getBoundingClientRect();\\n      const newW = Math.max(100, Math.floor(rect.width));\\n      const newH = Math.max(100, Math.floor(rect.height));\\n\\n      // CRITICAL: Only mutate canvas.width/height if dimensions strictly changed!\\n      // Assigning canvas.width / canvas.height unconditionally clears the entire buffer to blank.\\n      if (\\n        newW !== canvasSizeRef.current.width ||\\n        newH !== canvasSizeRef.current.height ||\\n        canvas.width !== newW ||\\n        canvas.height !== newH\\n      ) {\\n        canvasSizeRef.current = { width: newW, height: newH };\\n        canvas.width = newW;\\n        canvas.height = newH;\\n        setCanvasDimensions({ width: newW, height: newH });\\n        latestRef.current.requestRender(true);\\n\\n        // Auto adjust camera when switching between landscape and portrait\\n        const { entities, extents, onUpdateCamera } = latestRef.current;\\n        if (entities.length > 0) {\\n          const isPortrait = newW < newH;\\n          if (\\n            prevIsPortraitRef.current !== null &&\\n            prevIsPortraitRef.current !== isPortrait\\n          ) {\\n            const extW = Math.max(10, extents.maxX - extents.minX);\\n            const extH = Math.max(10, extents.maxY - extents.minY);\\n            const newCamX = (extents.minX + extents.maxX) / 2;\\n            const newCamY = (extents.minY + extents.maxY) / 2;\\n            const fittedZoom = Math.min((newW * 0.88) / extW, (newH * 0.88) / extH);\\n            onUpdateCamera(newCamX, newCamY, fittedZoom);\\n          }\\n          prevIsPortraitRef.current = isPortrait;\\n        }\\n      }\\n    };\\n\\n    handleResize();\\n\\n    const ro = new ResizeObserver(() => {\\n      handleResize();\\n    });\\n    ro.observe(container);\\n\\n    window.addEventListener(\'resize\', handleResize);\\n    window.addEventListener(\'orientationchange\', () => {\\n      setTimeout(handleResize, 100);\\n      setTimeout(handleResize, 350);\\n    });\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      ro.disconnect();\\n      window.removeEventListener(\'resize\', handleResize);\\n    };\\n  }, []);\", \"StartLine\":991, \"TargetContent\":\"  // Window & Container resize observer with orientation auto-adjustment\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const container = containerRef.current;\\n    if (!container) return;\\n\\n    let prevW = 0;\\n    let prevH = 0;\\n\\n    const handleResize = () => {\\n      const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n      if (!container || !canvas) return;\\n      const rect = container.getBoundingClientRect();\\n      const newW = Math.max(100, Math.floor(rect.width));\\n      const newH = Math.max(100, Math.floor(rect.height));\\n\\n      if (\\n        newW !== prevW ||\\n        newH !== prevH ||\\n        canvas.width !== newW ||\\n        canvas.height !== newH\\n      ) {\\n        prevW = newW;\\n        prevH = newH;\\n        canvas.width = newW;\\n        canvas.height = newH;\\n        setCanvasDimensions({ width: newW, height: newH });\\n\\n        // Auto adjust camera when switching between landscape and portrait!\\n        if (entities.length > 0) {\\n          const isPortrait = newW < newH;\\n          if (\\n            prevIsPortraitRef.current !== null &&\\n            prevIsPortraitRef.current !== isPortrait\\n          ) {\\n            const extW = Math.max(10, extents.maxX - extents.minX);\\n            const extH = Math.max(10, extents.maxY - extents.minY);\\n            const newCamX = (extents.minX + extents.maxX) / 2;\\n            const newCamY = (extents.minY + extents.maxY) / 2;\\n            const fittedZoom = Math.min((newW * 0.88) / extW, (newH * 0.88) / extH);\\n            onUpdateCamera(newCamX, newCamY, fittedZoom);\\n          }\\n          prevIsPortraitRef.current = isPortrait;\\n        }\\n      }\\n    };\\n\\n    handleResize();\\n\\n    const ro = new ResizeObserver(() => {\\n      handleResize();\\n    });\\n    ro.observe(container);\\n\\n    window.addEventListener(\'resize\', handleResize);\\n    window.addEventListener(\'orientationchange\', () => {\\n      setTimeout(handleResize, 100);\\n      setTimeout(handleResize, 350);\\n    });\\n    if (window.visualViewport) {\\n      window.visualViewport.addEventListener(\'resize\', handleResize);\\n    }\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      ro.disconnect();\\n      window.removeEventListener(\'resize\', handleResize);\\n      if (window.visualViewport) {\\n        window.visualViewport.removeEventListener(\'resize\', handleResize);\\n      }\\n    };\\n  }, [entities.length, extents, onUpdateCamera]);\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/CADCanvas.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Stabilizing resize observer effect\", \"toolSummary\":\"Prevent blanking canvas on resize and movement\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\255\024\n\252\024\001i\024}\023P\033\2450\2545\230@\202\230\343g\217\362k> \210@\316wD\337\247\023\252o\327\373\257y\n\252i\333\241] wf\327N\332\272-\006D\021\376Jb\320X\223\202\225s\2515\'\372\355E\305v\006\355\360\f^7\223\243eX\326\266\275>\241-\224d^\313\237\347a\312\314\326\311\236ZD\\\"K\241U\374\337I\201q_s`\274|\272\n\005\3525\260\327\226\030!V!\230[\343?\372\313p\221\326\273z\255s\200\372\345\023\254a\212\005ziS\325\224#\275\361;Q\364\364\367\341\3206\205\366\305\341\362\372\b\301q\025|U\316-\324\211)\376\257e\f\214@[\216\002\225\312\314d\315\317\244\3244\260gy\323Z3Z\2113#DeaAk\236\334\024\215\202\355Ci\241\000syBpQ\3112<\305U\327\323\017\365\302\315\362\365\222_qV,\201\3033\n\276>\244s\214ia\304\311t}\204\276\236/tE\235(\002\260\a\342\263\227e\225\323\337\255T\207l8\364\177\346\177\351\337\301\350.\223\b\263s]\245]\205\272g\325\003\3379I\243^}5\225)\344~\223mc<H\362S\361S\343\336\342!\352^\311\273J\273\036\251\346\316\016\n\301\206\224\2623\225\2031#\337;\023]\303\346\237\260D\332\311\257\367\271\016\306\022\032\024\264\024\341\302\221w\273+)\321\313@+\330\227\200i\254\321\305\301\026-\220\310\bl;5\016S\204>\304C\343c+_\"v>[IM\246P~\226\200y`\305\242\\\021P\254\332\261\333\220\303\301\267\342\031:\006\025:\332\332\364\212\034\000\001\0041\277\221\320\343\257n\306\237XD\344\262HN\210nm\220\357\245\020\225\304\302k\274h\311\3063K!Q\b;\f\363\276\246-\0176t\352T\224\360c\036\347\331\327\"i\034\240\272T\315\025\262o\026\203\250E\342\237o\266\232\343\3233\f\353\234ST\314\221|\374\361x\'\030\351\254\372\nX\321y\324\364z\030\231\264/\"\301\fa\320\006\031\216\257U\211\333t\255#T\314\357\301\016 \336\2327\327<\270\327N<m\000\355:\326\2428\352\332\370\327\234P\342\n>g\361\036F:\033*\371\373\276\366\224\364\016\353\271\256\353@\303b/F|M\r\215)\001&\244\020\216\3320\245\033P\341\314\vY\'vF\225\223\252\211i\000\223\033\255i[Nkt\357\004\312\267C\301\357\375\240.\214\031\331%q\215\250\364\240\347\262\333Eq \332>\312s\315\313\203y+\337\300l\