    thinking: "**Analyzing CAD Canvas Code**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `CADCanvas.tsx` component, specifically lines 698-747. I\'ve begun dissecting the logic within the `noRot` conditional block, paying close attention to the coordinate manipulation within the loop (lines 698-727). My goal is to understand how the code handles rotation and the implications of the `noRot` flag.\n\n\n**Investigating Edge Cases**\n\nI\'m now diving into the edge case handling within the coordinate processing loop. Specifically, I\'m examining the conditional statement starting with `if (adx > 80 && ady > 80 && Math.hypot(adx, ady) > 500)`. I want to understand why these conditions are used to filter out certain line segments, especially those diagonal streaks crossing between machines. I\'m also scrutinizing the viewport clipping logic, checking how it ensures lines stay within the canvas bounds.\n\n\n**Examining Polyline Rendering**\n\nI\'m now shifting my focus to the polyline rendering logic, specifically how vertices are processed and transformed from world coordinates to screen coordinates. I\'m scrutinizing the `worldToScreen` function and the checks for finite values to ensure valid coordinates. I want to understand how this impacts the visual representation of complex shapes, particularly with the `polys` data structure.\n\n\n**Scrutinizing Segment Anomalies**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down into the segment anomaly detection within the polyline rendering. I\'m focusing on those `segDx`, `segDy`, and `Math.hypot` calculations. I see how they\'re used to identify and handle large leaps in coordinates, presumably preventing undesirable visual artifacts, such as erroneous lines across the entire display. I\'m now verifying these rules are appropriate for the data and context.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_18076296801230188997"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Filter anomalous diagonal streak lines and polyline leaps during rendering in CADCanvas\", \"EndLine\":748, \"Instruction\":\"Add jump checks for lines and polylines during drawing to prevent streak lines across views\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"        if (noRot) {\\n          for (let i = 0; i < coords.length; i += 4) {\\n            const x1 = coords[i];\\n            const y1 = coords[i + 1];\\n            const x2 = coords[i + 2];\\n            const y2 = coords[i + 3];\\n            const adx = Math.abs(x2 - x1);\\n            const ady = Math.abs(y2 - y1);\\n            // Drop anomalous diagonal streaks crossing between machines/views\\n            if (adx > 80 && ady > 80 && Math.hypot(adx, ady) > 500) continue;\\n\\n            const sx1 = halfW + (x1 - camX) * zoom;\\n            const sy1 = halfH - (y1 - camY) * zoom;\\n            const sx2 = halfW + (x2 - camX) * zoom;\\n            const sy2 = halfH - (y2 - camY) * zoom;\\n            if (\\n              (sx1 < 0 && sx2 < 0) ||\\n              (sx1 > cw && sx2 > cw) ||\\n              (sy1 < 0 && sy2 < 0) ||\\n              (sy1 > ch && sy2 > ch)\\n            )\\n              continue;\\n            ctx.moveTo(sx1, sy1);\\n            ctx.lineTo(sx2, sy2);\\n          }\\n        } else {\\n          for (let i = 0; i < coords.length; i += 4) {\\n            const x1 = coords[i];\\n            const y1 = coords[i + 1];\\n            const x2 = coords[i + 2];\\n            const y2 = coords[i + 3];\\n            const adx = Math.abs(x2 - x1);\\n            const ady = Math.abs(y2 - y1);\\n            if (adx > 80 && ady > 80 && Math.hypot(adx, ady) > 500) continue;\\n\\n            const dx1 = x1 - camX;\\n            const dy1 = y1 - camY;\\n            const sx1 = halfW + (dx1 * cosA - dy1 * sinA) * zoom;\\n            const sy1 = halfH - (dx1 * sinA + dy1 * cosA) * zoom;\\n            const dx2 = x2 - camX;\\n            const dy2 = y2 - camY;\\n            const sx2 = halfW + (dx2 * cosA - dy2 * sinA) * zoom;\\n            const sy2 = halfH - (dx2 * sinA + dy2 * cosA) * zoom;\\n            ctx.moveTo(sx1, sy1);\\n            ctx.lineTo(sx2, sy2);\\n          }\\n        }\\n\\n        // Polylines\\n        const polys = batch.polylines;\\n        for (let pIdx = 0; pIdx < polys.length; pIdx++) {\\n          const verts = polys[pIdx].vertices;\\n          if (verts.length < 2) continue;\\n          const v0 = verts[0];\\n          if (!isFinite(v0.x) || !isFinite(v0.y)) continue;\\n          const s0 = worldToScreen(v0.x, v0.y);\\n          if (!isFinite(s0.x) || !isFinite(s0.y)) continue;\\n          ctx.moveTo(s0.x, s0.y);\\n          for (let k = 1; k < verts.length; k++) {\\n            const vk = verts[k];\\n            const vp = verts[k - 1];\\n            if (!isFinite(vk.x) || !isFinite(vk.y)) continue;\\n            const sk = worldToScreen(vk.x, vk.y);\\n            if (!isFinite(sk.x) || !isFinite(sk.y)) continue;\\n\\n            const segDx = Math.abs(vk.x - vp.x);\\n            const segDy = Math.abs(vk.y - vp.y);\\n            // If segment is an anomalous diagonal leap across views, jump instead of drawing a line\\n            if (segDx > 80 && segDy > 80 && Math.hypot(segDx, segDy) > 500) {\\n              ctx.moveTo(sk.x, sk.y);\\n            } else {\\n              ctx.lineTo(sk.x, sk.y);\\n            }\\n          }\\n          if (polys[pIdx].closed) {\\n            const lastV = verts[verts.length - 1];\\n            const cDx = Math.abs(lastV.x - v0.x);\\n            const cDy = Math.abs(lastV.y - v0.y);\\n            if (!(cDx > 80 && cDy > 80 && Math.hypot(cDx, cDy) > 500)) {\\n              ctx.closePath();\\n            }\\n          }\\n        }\", \"StartLine\":698, \"TargetContent\":\"        if (noRot) {\\n          for (let i = 0; i < coords.length; i += 4) {\\n            const sx1 = halfW + (coords[i] - camX) * zoom;\\n            const sy1 = halfH - (coords[i + 1] - camY) * zoom;\\n            const sx2 = halfW + (coords[i + 2] - camX) * zoom;\\n            const sy2 = halfH - (coords[i + 3] - camY) * zoom;\\n            if (\\n              (sx1 < 0 && sx2 < 0) ||\\n              (sx1 > cw && sx2 > cw) ||\\n              (sy1 < 0 && sy2 < 0) ||\\n              (sy1 > ch && sy2 > ch)\\n            )\\n              continue;\\n            ctx.moveTo(sx1, sy1);\\n            ctx.lineTo(sx2, sy2);\\n          }\\n        } else {\\n          for (let i = 0; i < coords.length; i += 4) {\\n            const dx1 = coords[i] - camX;\\n            const dy1 = coords[i + 1] - camY;\\n            const sx1 = halfW + (dx1 * cosA - dy1 * sinA) * zoom;\\n            const sy1 = halfH - (dx1 * sinA + dy1 * cosA) * zoom;\\n            const dx2 = coords[i + 2] - camX;\\n            const dy2 = coords[i + 3] - camY;\\n            const sx2 = halfW + (dx2 * cosA - dy2 * sinA) * zoom;\\n            const sy2 = halfH - (dx2 * sinA + dy2 * cosA) * zoom;\\n            ctx.moveTo(sx1, sy1);\\n            ctx.lineTo(sx2, sy2);\\n          }\\n        }\\n\\n        // Polylines\\n        const polys = batch.polylines;\\n        for (let pIdx = 0; pIdx < polys.length; pIdx++) {\\n          const verts = polys[pIdx].vertices;\\n          if (verts.length < 2) continue;\\n          const v0 = verts[0];\\n          if (!isFinite(v0.x) || !isFinite(v0.y)) continue;\\n          const s0 = worldToScreen(v0.x, v0.y);\\n          if (!isFinite(s0.x) || !isFinite(s0.y)) continue;\\n          ctx.moveTo(s0.x, s0.y);\\n          for (let k = 1; k < verts.length; k++) {\\n            const vk = verts[k];\\n            if (!isFinite(vk.x) || !isFinite(vk.y)) continue;\\n            const sk = worldToScreen(vk.x, vk.y);\\n            if (!isFinite(sk.x) || !isFinite(sk.y)) continue;\\n            ctx.lineTo(sk.x, sk.y);\\n          }\\n          if (polys[pIdx].closed) ctx.closePath();\\n        }\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/CADCanvas.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Adding streak filtering to line and polyline rendering\", \"toolSummary\":\"Filter diagonal streaks in line and polyline draw\"}"
