  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 3
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **User Request**:\n     1. \"1 \353\262\210 \354\202\254\354\247\204\352\271\214\354\247\204 \352\264\234\354\260\256\354\235\200\353\215\260 2\353\262\210 \354\202\254\354\247\204\354\262\230\353\237\274 \354\242\200\353\215\224 \355\231\225\353\214\200\355\225\230\353\251\264 \352\270\264\354\204\240\353\223\244\354\235\264 \354\203\235\352\262\250\" (Zooming in creates long abnormal diagonal white lines connecting separate machines/views).\n     2. \"\352\267\270\353\246\254\352\263\240 \355\231\224\353\251\264 \354\235\264\353\217\231\354\213\234 \355\231\224\353\251\264 \352\271\234\353\271\241\354\236\204\354\235\264\354\236\210\354\234\274\353\213\210 \355\225\264\352\262\260\355\225\264\" (Screen flickering occurs during screen panning/moving).\n   - **Success Criteria**:\n     - Completely eliminate the anomalous diagonal streak lines that appear across drawing views when zooming or panning.\n     - Eliminate the screen flickering during pan/drag/touch moves while preserving smooth 60fps/120fps motion.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Root Causes Identified & Fixed**:\n     1. **Root Cause of Screen Flickering on Pan/Move**:\n        - In `App.tsx`, `onUpdateCamera={(nx, ny, nz) => ...}` was an inline arrow function re-created on every render.\n        - In `src/components/CADCanvas.tsx`, the `ResizeObserver` `useEffect` had `[entities.length, extents, onUpdateCamera]` as dependencies.\n        - Every pixel of panning triggered an `onUpdateCamera` call, causing `App.tsx` to re-render, changing the function identity and re-running the resize `useEffect`.\n        - Inside the resize effect, `prevW` and `prevH` were reset to 0, which evaluated `newW !== prevW` as true, unconditionally re-assigning `canvas.width = newW` and `canvas.height = newH`. In HTML5 Canvas, setting `canvas.width`/`height` immediately wipes the canvas buffer to transparent/blank on every single pixel moved.\n        - Additionally, `cancelAnimationFrame` in the reactive `useEffect` cleanup was canceling in-flight render frames mid-drag.\n        - **Fix**: Wrapped `handleUpdateCamera` in `useCallback` in `src/App.tsx`. In `src/components/CADCanvas.tsx`, introduced `canvasSizeRef` to only set `canvas.width`/`canvas.height` when dimensions strictly change, removed `window.visualViewport` resize listener, and changed the resize `useEffect` dependency array to `[]`. Removed premature `cancelAnimationFrame` from the prop-update cleanup.\n     2. **Root Cause of Long Anomalous Diagonal Lines on Zoom/Pan**:\n        - In `src/lib/dxfParser.ts`, `SPLINE` entities treated group codes 12/22 and 13/23 (tangent direction vectors like `(0, -1)` or `(1, 0)`) as coordinates and pushed them as polyline vertices alongside control/fit points, creating long diagonal streak lines to the origin.\n        - In `src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts`, DWG `SPLINE` entities had tangent vectors or distant `(0, 0)` origin leaps appended at the ends of fit/control points.\n        - In `src/lib/modelExpander.ts`, `isArtifactStreakSegment` required `dx > 350 && dy > 350`, missing shallow diagonal leaps (`dy < 350` or connection to origin `(0, 0)`).\n        - In `src/components/CADCanvas.tsx`, batch rendering did not check for anomalous diagonal leaps between vertices during drawing.\n        - **Fix**:\n          - `src/lib/dxfParser.ts`: Separated `fitPoints` and `controlPoints`, ignored tangent vector codes 12/22 and 13/23.\n          - `src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts`: Filtered trailing/leading tangent vectors and stray origin leaps at the ends of splines.\n          - `src/lib/modelExpander.ts`: Strengthened `isArtifactStreakSegment` to drop any origin leaps (`len > 250` near origin), diagonal streaks (`dx > 80 && dy > 80 && len > 500`), and non-axis-aligned segments (`len > 1200`).\n          - `src/components/CADCanvas.tsx`: Added runtime jump filtering in `batch.lineCoords` and converted polyline leap segments (`segDx > 80 && segDy > 80 && len > 500`) from `ctx.lineTo` to `ctx.moveTo` so leaps across views are never drawn. Also guarded `ctx.closePath()`.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - Assigning `canvas.width` or `canvas.height` in HTML5 2D Canvas clears the entire raster surface synchronously. Any hook re-evaluating during drag that touches `canvas.width` causes alternate-frame black/white flashing.\n   - DXF/DWG splines frequently store starting and ending tangent vectors (codes 12/22, 13/23). Treating them as polyline vertices connects machine parts to near-origin points, which visually cuts across the entire drawing when zooming or panning.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - All code edits across `src/lib/dxfParser.ts`, `src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts`, `src/lib/modelExpander.ts`, `src/App.tsx`, and `src/components/CADCanvas.tsx` have been applied.\n   - Build verification with `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` is the immediate next step.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Modified files:\n     - `/src/lib/dxfParser.ts`\n     - `/src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts`\n     - `/src/lib/modelExpander.ts`\n     - `/src/App.tsx`\n     - `/src/components/CADCanvas.tsx`\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. Execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together in a single call to verify that TypeScript compilation and lint checks pass cleanly.\n   2. If any compile or lint errors occur, fix them immediately.\n   3. Call `restart_dev_server` to ensure the dev server serves the updated bundle.\n   4. Provide a concise, clear response to the user explaining:\n      - How the long diagonal streak lines on zoom were traced to spline tangent vector points and cross-view polyline leaps, and how they were filtered.\n      - How the flickering during screen movement was traced to resize observer re-execution clearing the canvas buffer on camera updates, and how it was stabilized with `canvasSizeRef` and callback memoization.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - React SPA on Vite, Tailwind CSS, TypeScript.\n   - No mock data or fake fallbacks.\n   - Response to the user must be concise, polite, and in Korean.\n</summary>"
