  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Rendering Issues**\n\nI\'ve been examining the re-rendering behavior. I\'ve realized `App.tsx` was re-rendering every `onUpdateCamera` trigger because the inline function wasn\'t memoized. This caused `CADCanvas` to re-render, as well, which led to inefficient resize operations. I\'m focusing on optimization strategies now.\n\n\n**Optimizing Resize Behavior**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the root cause! The `useEffect`\'s dependency array caused excessive re-renders and resize operations on *every* mouse/touch move, destroying and recreating the observer, and resetting canvas dimensions to 0. This frequent clearing was then exacerbated by the `cancelAnimationFrame` call in the cleanup, causing that flashing. I\'ve now memoized `handleUpdateCamera` and I\'m moving on to `CADCanvas.tsx`.\n\n\n**Confirming Flicker-Free Rendering**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the resize `useEffect`\'s dependency array is correctly set to `[]`, ensuring it only mounts once. The `canvasSizeRef` tracks actual dimension changes efficiently. The double-buffering and `requestAnimationFrame` coalescing guarantee flicker-free rendering at 60/120fps. This handles panning and pinching seamlessly. Now, I\'m focusing on the zooming issue and investigating the user\'s images.\n\n\n"
