  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Deployment Options**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on the deployment aspect. I\'m considering the user\'s specific request for private distribution, bypassing the Google Play Store. My goal is to determine the simplest and most effective approach that satisfies those criteria. I am weighing options such as direct APK sharing or perhaps utilizing some kind of limited distribution platform.\n\n\n**Exploring Direct Sharing Solutions**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the AI Studio shared URL. It seems like the most immediate and user-friendly path for private distribution. Direct sharing via that link seems a smart option. I am trying to better understand how to make the installation on a mobile device seamless for the end-user. The PWA aspect is very interesting, and I like that it\'s a completely self-contained method.\n\n\n**Evaluating Offline Accessibility**\n\nI\'m now investigating an offline distribution method. Downloading a single HTML file and distributing it directly seems ideal for total personal control, allowing usage without internet connectivity. I am also considering creating an Android APK file for those who need it, possibly through PWABuilder, for distribution via KakaoTalk or email.\n\n\n**Refining Distribution Methods**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the distribution methods. I am exploring the possibility of allowing installation of pure Android apps without the Play Store by enabling external app installations. The GitHub Pages option also looks attractive, potentially providing a personal domain for the app through auto-deployment. I also want to check the `DeployModal.tsx` file for the possibility of generating a QR code or providing a copy-link button for easy sharing via KakaoTalk or other platforms.\n\n\n"
