  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Phantom Lines**\n\nI\'m focusing intently on those pesky phantom long lines that pop up when DXF files are opened in real CAD. Despite implementing filters, the issue persists. My priority now is to thoroughly investigate every potential cause for the appearance of these non-existent lines within DXF files. I\'m aiming to find where the error is occurring in processing.\n\n\n**Analyzing Large File Failures**\n\nI\'m now deeply engaged in understanding why large CAD files are failing to load or are missing entities. My attention has turned towards potential bottlenecks. I\'m scrutinizing `src/lib/dxfParser.ts`, `src/lib/libreDwgLoader.ts`, `src/lib/modelExpander.ts`, and `src/lib/cadSanitizer.ts`. Memory limits, the `MAX_ENTITIES` constant, and string splitting during file parsing are primary areas of concern and investigation.\n\n\n**Examining DWG Loading**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of DWG parsing. My goal is to pinpoint how DWG files are loaded and converted, and to look for specific areas of the process that may relate to the large file failures.\n\n\n"
