  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Initial State**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `App.tsx`\'s initialization. I see the `model` state is set to `null` initially. The `useEffect` hook, on mount, appears to only fetch recent drawings, it doesn\'t immediately populate the model itself. My aim is to understand the implications of this approach.\n\n\n**Addressing Active Session Persistence**\n\nI\'ve realized the critical flaw: the active drawing wasn\'t being preserved across browser sessions or refreshes. The `model`\'s in-memory state was lost. I\'m now exploring solutions. IndexedDB seems ideal for persistently storing the active drawing\'s ID, along with camera data and a timestamp. On app startup, I\'ll check for an active session in IndexedDB and restore it, also listening to visibility changes to sync.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
