    thinking: "**Analyzing Drawing Criteria**\n\nI\'ve been examining specific lines in `CADCanvas.tsx`, particularly 711 and 741. Focusing on the condition `(adx > 80 && ady > 80 && aLen > 500)`, I\'m considering scenarios where these criteria apply to actual diagonal machine lines within a drawing. This could include trusses, angled supports, or inclined frames.\n\n\n**Refining Line Rendering**\n\nI\'ve determined that the initial filtering condition `adx > 80 && ady > 80 && aLen > 500` was excessively restrictive, inadvertently hiding crucial diagonal lines, such as inclined machine parts or dimension lines. I\'m now revising this. I believe that only origin leaps should be dropped. I\'m carefully analyzing the screenshot (`image_e57460e2.png`) to understand why some lines were rendered and identifying the entities creating those long radiating lines; I\'m investigating `SPLINE` fits and their properties.\n\n\n**Investigating Entity Relationships**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of entity interactions within the parsing process. I\'m focusing on scenarios where tangents are appended in DXF or where coordinate system references are present. Specifically, I\'m examining how POLYLINE mesh vertices and their indices are handled to avoid misinterpretations that lead to incorrect line connections. I also am looking into DWG anonymous dimension blocks that may result in long connecting lines and their relationship with `DEFPOINTS`. Finally, I\'m paying attention to `LEADER` entities.\n\n\n**Addressing Parsing Artifacts**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on parsing inaccuracies. I believe that incorrectly parsed vertices, especially those near text annotations, are creating connection artifacts. I\'ve found a critical issue where the presence of the annotation target, like `(0, 0)`, in the vertex list leads to an unwanted connection to the origin. To address this, I\'m implementing a low-memory, line-by-line scanner for DXF in `dxfParser.ts`. I also plan to filter out certain records and entities, such as face records and DEFPOINTS. Similar improvements are planned in `libreDwgLoader.ts` to ensure all objects, including those in model space, are visible.\n\n\n"
