  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Line Scanner**\n\nI\'m working on the `dxfParser.ts` file. My latest focus is incorporating a fast, zero-duplication line scanner within `parseDxfText`. This is intended to prevent potential out-of-memory errors when dealing with extremely large DXF files. I\'m starting by defining the `pairs` array and getting the length of the `dxfText`.\n\n\n**Refining Line Scanning Logic**\n\nI\'ve refined the `scanLine` function to handle potential edge cases with carriage returns. I\'m focusing on skipping the \'\\r\' character when it precedes a newline. This should lead to more robust parsing. Additionally, I\'m now integrating this updated scanning logic within the `POLYLINE` section, specifically to process vertex data more effectively. I\'m continuing to refine its performance.\n\n\n"
