    thinking: "**Examining Relevant Imports**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the imports within `src/App.tsx`. I see several functions related to managing recent drawings: retrieving them, saving, loading, deleting, and clearing them, as well as saving active drawing sessions. This indicates the central role of this component in managing the application\'s drawing history and state.\n\n\n**Analyzing Camera State Management**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation details for camera state, especially how it\'s saved and restored. I see `cameraStateRef` and `currentModelRef` being used to maintain current values. A `useEffect` hook loads the recent drawings and the active drawing session on initial mount. This also includes restoring the camera position if a session is found. There\'s also a debounced camera saving mechanism. I\'m focusing on the interplay of these mechanisms now.\n\n\n**Investigating Camera Saving Logic**\n\nI\'m now focused on the camera state saving mechanisms. There\'s a `useEffect` hook that saves the active camera state with a 500ms delay, triggered by camera parameter changes, and I am also looking at how the state is saved when the window/tab loses focus, including handling visibility changes and page unload events. This seems robust, but I am still investigating how these interact with other camera state updates.\n\n\n"
